{"task_id": "django_000", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "c0-bare", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "The relevant `Article` is defined in [tests/model_options/models/tablespaces.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/tests/model_options/models/tablespaces.py:33). Its tablespace behavior depends on three layers: model/field configuration, database routing during migrations, and backend tablespace support.\n\n- The Article table itself requests `tbl_tbsp` through `Meta.db_tablespace`. Its physical table name is explicitly `model_options_articleref`.\n- The `code` field requests `idx_tbsp` for its unique index through `db_tablespace=\"idx_tbsp\"`.\n- The `title` field has no field-level tablespace. Its unique index therefore falls back first to `DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE`, and then to the model\u2019s `tbl_tbsp`. This precedence is implemented by `BaseDatabaseSchemaEditor._get_index_tablespace_sql()` in [django/db/backends/base/schema.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/db/backends/base/schema.py:1541).\n- The implicit primary-key index follows the same default-index/model-tablespace fallback. `Field.db_tablespace` itself resolves an unspecified field setting to `settings.DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE` in [django/db/models/fields/__init__.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:961).\n- `authors` has no explicit field tablespace. Its automatically generated join table inherits Article\u2019s `tbl_tbsp`, while its indexes use `DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE` when configured, otherwise `tbl_tbsp`.\n- `reviewers` explicitly sets `db_tablespace=\"idx_tbsp\"`. Its join table still inherits Article\u2019s `tbl_tbsp`, but the two foreign-key indexes use `idx_tbsp`. The implicit-through-model construction and propagation are in [django/db/models/fields/related.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/db/models/fields/related.py:1411).\n\nThe global defaults are empty unless overridden:\n\n- `DEFAULT_TABLESPACE = \"\"`\n- `DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE = \"\"`\n\nThese are defined in [django/conf/global_settings.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/conf/global_settings.py:435). `Options.__init__()` initializes a model\u2019s `db_tablespace` from `DEFAULT_TABLESPACE` before an explicit `Meta.db_tablespace` replaces it, in [django/db/models/options.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/db/models/options.py:140).\n\nDatabase routing gates whether any of this reaches a particular database. `CreateModel.database_forwards()` calls `allow_migrate_model(connection_alias, model)` before invoking `schema_editor.create_model()` in [django/db/migrations/operations/models.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/db/migrations/operations/models.py:97). That wrapper:\n\n1. Rejects proxy, swapped, or unmanaged models through `Options.can_migrate()`.\n2. Then delegates to the configured routers\u2019 `allow_migrate()` with the model\u2019s app label, model name, and model object.\n\nSee [django/db/migrations/operations/base.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/db/migrations/operations/base.py:148) and [django/db/utils.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/db/utils.py:271). Consequently, the router chooses which database would receive Article\u2019s tablespace-bearing DDL; the tablespace names must exist and be usable on every database to which migration is allowed.\n\nThere is an additional dependency specific to this test model: `Article.Meta.managed = False`. Therefore normal migration processing rejects it before consulting the router. The source comment explains that this is intentional because the test database has no configured tablespaces; tests temporarily make these models managed while inspecting generated SQL.\n\nFinally, actual enforcement depends on the selected database backend:\n\n- Base backends declare `supports_tablespaces = False` and `tablespace_sql()` returns an empty string, so tablespace declarations are ignored: [django/db/backends/base/features.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/db/backends/base/features.py:126) and [django/db/backends/base/operations.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/db/backends/base/operations.py:523).\n- PostgreSQL and Oracle declare tablespace support and generate either `TABLESPACE <name>` or inline `USING INDEX TABLESPACE <name>` clauses: [PostgreSQL features](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/db/backends/postgresql/features.py:27), [PostgreSQL operations](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/db/backends/postgresql/operations.py:235), [Oracle features](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/db/backends/oracle/features.py:34), and [Oracle operations](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/db/backends/oracle/operations.py:573).\n\nThus Django only selects and emits the requested tablespace names. The routed database backend must support tablespaces, and the underlying database administrator must already have created them and granted the connection user sufficient permissions.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 9, "relevance": 10, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 38279, "output_tokens": 2227, "total_tokens": 40506, "cache_read_tokens": 139776, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 5, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["django/conf/global_settings.py", "django/db/backends/base/features.py", "django/db/backends/base/operations.py", "django/db/backends/base/schema.py", "django/db/backends/oracle/features.py", "django/db/backends/oracle/operations.py", "django/db/backends/postgresql/features.py", "django/db/backends/postgresql/operations.py", "django/db/migrations/operations/base.py", "django/db/migrations/operations/models.py", "django/db/models/fields/__init__.py", "django/db/models/fields/related.py", "django/db/models/options.py", "django/db/utils.py", "docs/topics/db/tablespaces.txt", "tests/model_options/models/tablespaces.py", "tests/model_options/test_tablespaces.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "c0-bare", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "c0-bare", "server_name": null, "launch_command": null, "launch_args": null, "served_tools": null, "client_tools": [], "index": null, "shares_index_with": null, "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-c0-bare-django-django"}, "served_tools": [], "served_count": null, "mcp_tools_issued": [], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": null, "mcp_per_server": {}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {}, "models_used": ["gpt-5.6-sol"], "prompt_style": "neutral", "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "wall_clock_seconds": 73.50807929039001, "index_time_seconds": 0.0, "judge_time_seconds": 4.721297979354858, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.08759075000000001, "error": null, "timed_out": false, "retries": 0, "timestamp": "2026-08-05T13:37:06.530058+00:00", "prompt_sent": "Answer the following question about this code repository.\nBe specific and reference actual code files and functions.\n\nQUESTION: What are the tablespace configuration dependencies of the Article class that interact with Django's database routing and the underlying database system's tablespace management capabilities?\n\nThink step by step. Use the available tools to explore the codebase.", "model_used": "gpt-5.6-sol", "session_id": "", "stop_reason": "", "duration_api_ms": 73505, "repo_commit": "3b161e60964a", "raw_output_file": "logs\\layerb_codex_bakeoff_django\\raw_outputs\\django_000_c0-bare.json"}
{"task_id": "django_000", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "repowise", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "The relevant `Article` is in [tests/model_options/models/tablespaces.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/tests/model_options/models/tablespaces.py:33). Its tablespace behavior depends on four layers:\n\n- Model configuration:\n  - `Meta.db_tablespace = \"tbl_tbsp\"` places the `Article` table in `tbl_tbsp`.\n  - `code` is `unique=True` with `db_tablespace=\"idx_tbsp\"`, so its unique index explicitly targets `idx_tbsp`.\n  - `title` is unique but has no field tablespace, so its index falls back to `DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE`, then the model\u2019s `db_tablespace`.\n  - `reviewers` specifies `db_tablespace=\"idx_tbsp\"`; `authors` does not.\n  - `Meta.db_table` points at the reference table, and `managed = False` prevents normal migration/schema management because the test database may not contain these named tablespaces.\n\n- Settings and option resolution:\n  - `Options.db_tablespace` defaults to `settings.DEFAULT_TABLESPACE` in [django/db/models/options.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/django/db/models/options.py:140), but `Article.Meta` overrides it with `tbl_tbsp`.\n  - A field\u2019s `db_tablespace` resolves as its explicit value or `settings.DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE` in [django/db/models/fields/__init__.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:961).\n  - Both global defaults are empty by default in [django/conf/global_settings.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/django/conf/global_settings.py:435). They are evaluated when the model class is constructed, which is why the tests say `override_settings()` cannot change them afterward.\n\n- Database routing and migrations:\n  - Migration operations first call `model._meta.can_migrate()`. This rejects unmanaged models before consulting the router; otherwise `router.allow_migrate_model()` is called in [django/db/migrations/operations/base.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/django/db/migrations/operations/base.py:148).\n  - The router passes `app_label`, `model_name`, and the model itself as a hint in [django/db/utils.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/django/db/utils.py:271). Thus routing decides which database may receive `Article`; it does not choose or validate the tablespace.\n  - The test temporarily changes `Article`, `Scientist`, and both through models to `managed=True` solely while collecting schema SQL in [tests/model_options/test_tablespaces.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/tests/model_options/test_tablespaces.py:34).\n\n- Backend capabilities:\n  - `BaseDatabaseSchemaEditor.create_model()` appends `ops.tablespace_sql(model._meta.db_tablespace)` to table creation in [django/db/backends/base/schema.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/django/db/backends/base/schema.py:302).\n  - Index placement follows: explicit field tablespace \u2192 `DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE` \u2192 model tablespace in `_get_index_tablespace_sql()` at [django/db/backends/base/schema.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/django/db/backends/base/schema.py:1541).\n  - Auto-created many-to-many through tables inherit `Article._meta.db_tablespace`, while their foreign-key indexes receive the `ManyToManyField` tablespace in [django/db/models/fields/related.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/django/db/models/fields/related.py:1412).\n  - Tablespaces are non-standard and unsupported by default: `supports_tablespaces = False`, and base `tablespace_sql()` returns an empty string. PostgreSQL and Oracle opt in and generate `TABLESPACE ...` or inline `USING INDEX TABLESPACE ...`.\n  - Consequently, unsupported backends silently omit the tablespace clauses, as verified by `test_tablespace_ignored_for_indexed_field()`. On PostgreSQL or Oracle, `tbl_tbsp` and `idx_tbsp` must actually exist and be usable by the database user; this schema code references or moves objects between tablespaces but does not provision those tablespaces for `Article`.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 9, "relevance": 10, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 39202, "output_tokens": 2191, "total_tokens": 41393, "cache_read_tokens": 164864, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 5, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["django/conf/global_settings.py", "django/db/backends/base/features.py", "django/db/backends/base/operations.py", "django/db/backends/base/schema.py", "django/db/backends/oracle/operations.py", "django/db/backends/postgresql/operations.py", "django/db/migrations/operations/base.py", "django/db/models/fields/__init__.py", "django/db/models/fields/related.py", "django/db/models/options.py", "django/db/utils.py", "tests/model_options/models/tablespaces.py", "tests/model_options/test_tablespaces.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": ["mcp__repowise__get_answer"], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "repowise", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "repowise", "server_name": "repowise", "launch_command": "C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/repowise-layerb/.venv/Scripts/repowise.exe", "launch_args": ["mcp", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-repowise-full-django-django", "--transport", "stdio"], "served_tools": null, "client_tools": ["mcp__repowise__get_answer", "mcp__repowise__get_context", "mcp__repowise__get_overview", "mcp__repowise__get_risk", "mcp__repowise__get_symbol", "mcp__repowise__get_why", "mcp__repowise__search_codebase"], "index": null, "shares_index_with": "repowise-full", "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeof