{"task_id": "django_000", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "codegraph", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "`Article`\u2019s tablespace behavior depends on three layers: model metadata, database routing/migration eligibility, and backend tablespace support.\n\n- In [tests/model_options/models/tablespaces.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/tests/model_options/models/tablespaces.py:33), `Article` declares:\n\n  - `Meta.db_tablespace = \"tbl_tbsp\"` for the article table.\n  - `code(..., unique=True, db_tablespace=\"idx_tbsp\")`, placing its unique index in `idx_tbsp`.\n  - `reviewers(..., db_tablespace=\"idx_tbsp\")`, placing indexes on that many-to-many relation in `idx_tbsp`.\n  - `authors` has no field tablespace, so its indexes inherit the normal fallback configuration.\n\n- Tablespace precedence is implemented by `BaseDatabaseSchemaEditor._get_index_tablespace_sql()` in [django/db/backends/base/schema.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/django/db/backends/base/schema.py:1541):\n\n  1. An explicitly supplied index tablespace.\n  2. A single field\u2019s `db_tablespace`.\n  3. `settings.DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE`.\n  4. The model\u2019s `Meta.db_tablespace`.\n\n  Thus `code` and the `reviewers` relation use `idx_tbsp`; ordinary indexes, including those for `authors`, use `DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE` when configured, otherwise `tbl_tbsp`.\n\n- Table creation uses `model._meta.db_tablespace` and delegates SQL generation to `connection.ops.tablespace_sql()` in [django/db/backends/base/schema.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/django/db/backends/base/schema.py:302). Inline unique constraints similarly use `field.db_tablespace` or the model tablespace, but only when `connection.features.supports_tablespaces` is true (`_iter_column_sql()`, around line 369).\n\n- Backend capability is decisive. The base feature flag defaults to `False` in [django/db/backends/base/features.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/django/db/backends/base/features.py:128), while PostgreSQL and Oracle set it to `True`. Their operations classes translate the selection into backend-specific `TABLESPACE` or `USING INDEX TABLESPACE` clauses. Unsupported backends effectively ignore the configuration, as demonstrated by `test_tablespace_ignored_*()` in [tests/model_options/test_tablespaces.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/tests/model_options/test_tablespaces.py:70).\n\n- Migration routing is a separate gate. `ConnectionRouter.allow_migrate_model()` passes the complete model in router hints in [django/db/utils.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/django/db/utils.py:271). Also, `Options.can_migrate()` rejects unmanaged models before considering backend requirements in [django/db/models/options.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/django/db/models/options.py:395). `Article` is normally `managed = False`, specifically because the ordinary test database may not have the named tablespaces. The tablespace tests temporarily set `Article` and its generated join models to managed so schema SQL can be exercised.\n\nIn short: routing and `managed` status decide whether `Article` is eligible for schema operations; model, field, and global settings decide which tablespace wins; and `supports_tablespaces` plus `ops.tablespace_sql()` decide whether\u2014and how\u2014the underlying database emits tablespace SQL.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 8, "reasoning": 8, "clarity": 9, "relevance": 9}, "input_tokens": 29396, "output_tokens": 2118, "total_tokens": 31514, "cache_read_tokens": 178176, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 12, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["django\\\\db\\\\backends\\\\base\\\\features.py", "django\\\\db\\\\backends\\\\base\\\\schema.py", "django\\\\db\\\\backends\\\\postgresql\\\\operations.py", "django\\\\db\\\\models\\\\options.py", "django\\\\db\\\\utils.py", "tests\\\\model_options\\\\models\\\\tablespaces.py", "tests\\\\model_options\\\\test_tablespaces.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "codegraph", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "codegraph", "server_name": "codegraph", "launch_command": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm/codegraph.cmd", "launch_args": ["serve", "--mcp", "--path", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django", "--no-watch"], "served_tools": null, "client_tools": ["mcp__codegraph__codegraph_explore"], "index": {"command": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm/codegraph.cmd", "init", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django"], "timeout_seconds": 10800}, "shares_index_with": null, "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django"}, "served_tools": ["codegraph_explore"], "served_count": 1, "mcp_tools_issued": ["mcp__codegraph__codegraph_explore", "mcp__codegraph__codegraph_explore"], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": true, "mcp_per_server": {"codegraph": {"ok": 2, "error": 0}}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {"arm": "codegraph", "rc": 0, "seconds": 2.6, "argv": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm/codegraph.cmd", "init", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django"], "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django"}, "models_used": ["gpt-5.6-sol"], "prompt_style": "neutral", "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "wall_clock_seconds": 80.91682982444763, "index_time_seconds": 2.6, "judge_time_seconds": 5.82702112197876, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.080197, "error": null, "timed_out": false, "retries": 0, "timestamp": "2026-08-05T13:40:08.479005+00:00", "prompt_sent": "Answer the following question about this code repository.\nBe specific and reference actual code files and functions.\n\nQUESTION: What are the tablespace configuration dependencies of the Article class that interact with Django's database routing and the underlying database system's tablespace management capabilities?\n\nThink step by step. Use the available tools to explore the codebase.", "model_used": "gpt-5.6-sol", "session_id": "", "stop_reason": "", "duration_api_ms": 80915, "repo_commit": "3b161e60964a", "raw_output_file": "logs\\layerb_codex_bakeoff_django\\raw_outputs\\django_000_codegraph.json"}
{"task_id": "django_000", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "graphify", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "`Article` has three layers of tablespace dependency: model/field configuration, database routing, and backend/database support.\n\n- In [tests/model_options/models/tablespaces.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/tests/model_options/models/tablespaces.py:33), `Article.Meta.db_tablespace = \"tbl_tbsp\"` places the main table in `tbl_tbsp`. The unique `code` field explicitly uses `db_tablespace=\"idx_tbsp\"`, and the `reviewers` many-to-many relation also specifies `idx_tbsp`. `title` and `authors` have no field-level override.\n\n- Django\u2019s defaults participate through `Options.db_tablespace`, initialized from `settings.DEFAULT_TABLESPACE` in [django/db/models/options.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/models/options.py:140), and `Field.db_tablespace`, which resolves to the explicit value or `settings.DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE` in [django/db/models/fields/__init__.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:961). For generated indexes, the priority is:\n  `explicit index/field tablespace \u2192 DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE \u2192 model db_tablespace`\n  ([django/db/backends/base/schema.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/backends/base/schema.py:1541)).\n\n- Database routing gates whether any schema operation occurs. Migration operations first reject models for which `_meta.can_migrate()` is false, then call `router.allow_migrate_model(connection_alias, model)` ([django/db/migrations/operations/base.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/migrations/operations/base.py:148)). The router supplies the database alias, app label, model name, and model to configured routers ([django/db/utils.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/utils.py:257)). Thus routing decides which database receives the DDL; it does not translate or select tablespace names.\n\n- `Article` is specifically declared `managed = False`. Consequently, `Options.can_migrate()` rejects it before router approval ([django/db/models/options.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/models/options.py:395)). The tests temporarily set it to managed only to generate schema SQL. It also shares `model_options_articleref` with the reference model so other migrations do not attempt tablespace-backed table creation.\n\n- Backend capability is exposed by `connection.features.supports_tablespaces`, which defaults to `False` ([django/db/backends/base/features.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/backends/base/features.py:126)). Unsupported backends return an empty string from `DatabaseOperations.tablespace_sql()`, effectively ignoring the configuration ([django/db/backends/base/operations.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/backends/base/operations.py:523)). PostgreSQL and Oracle declare support and emit `TABLESPACE ...` or inline `USING INDEX TABLESPACE ...` clauses.\n\n- Finally, Django only emits references to `\"tbl_tbsp\"` and `\"idx_tbsp\"`; it does not provision them. They must already exist and be usable by the database account. The fixture explicitly notes that the test database has no tablespaces, which is why these models are unmanaged. The supported/unsupported behavior is verified in [tests/model_options/test_tablespaces.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/tests/model_options/test_tablespaces.py:59).\n\nIn short: routing determines whether `Article` may be migrated on a connection, backend features determine whether tablespace clauses can be emitted, settings and explicit model/field options determine which names are emitted, and the underlying database administrator must provide those tablespaces and permissions.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 9, "relevance": 10, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 46703, "output_tokens": 2424, "total_tokens": 49127, "cache_read_tokens": 291328, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 8, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["/schema.py", "django/db/backends/base/features.py", "django/db/backends/base/operations.py", "django/db/backends/base/schema.py", "django/db/migrations/operations/base.py", "django/db/migrations/operations/models.py", "django/db/models/fields/__init__.py", "django/db/models/options.py", "django/db/utils.py", "tests/model_options/models/tablespaces.py", "tests/model_options/test_tablespaces.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "graphify", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "graphify", "server_name": "graphify", "launch_command": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/graphify-mcp.exe", "launch_args": ["--transport", "stdio", "--graph", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-graphify-django-django/graphify-out/graph.json"], "served_tools": null, "client_tools": ["mcp__graphify__query_graph", "mcp__graphify__get_node", "mcp__graphify__get_neighbors", "mcp__graphify__shortest_path", "mcp__graphify__get_community", "mcp__graphify__god_nodes", "mcp__graphify__graph_stats"], "index": {"command": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/graphify.exe", "update", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-graphify-django-django"], "timeout_seconds": 10800}, "shares_index_with": null, "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-graphify-django-django"}, "served_tools": ["get_community", "get_neighbors", "get_node", "get_pr_impact", "god_nodes", "graph_stats", "list_prs", "query_graph", "shortest_path", "triage_prs"], "served_count": 10, "mcp_tools_issued": ["mcp__graphify__query_graph"], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": true, "mcp_per_server": {"graphify": {"ok": 1, "error": 0}}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {"arm": "graphify", "rc": 0, "seconds": 167.4, "argv": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/graphify.exe", "update", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-graphify-django-django"], "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-graphify-django-django"}, "models_used": ["gpt-5.6-sol"], "prompt_style": "neutral", "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "wall_clock_seconds": 119.56335186958313, "index_time_seconds": 167.4, "judge_time_seconds": 4.372690916061401, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.11903475, "error": null, "timed_out": false, "retries": 0, "timestamp": "2026-08-05T13:41:40.880618+00:00", "prompt_sent": "Answer the following question about this code repository.\nBe specific and reference actual code files and functions.\n\nQUESTION: What are the tablespace configuration dependencies of the Article class that interact with Django's database routing and the underlying database system's tablespace management capabilities?\n\nThink step by step. Use the available tools to explore the codebase.", "model_used": "gpt-5.6-sol", "session_id": "", "stop_reason": "", "duration_api_ms": 119561, "repo_commit": "3b161e60964a", "raw_output_file": "logs\\layerb_codex_bakeoff_django\\raw_outputs\\django_000_graphify.json"}
{"task_id": "django_000", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "code-review-graph", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "The relevant `Article` is defined in [tests/model_options/models/tablespaces.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/tests/model_options/models/tablespaces.py:33). Its tablespace behavior depends on four layers:\n\n- Model/table configuration: `Article.Meta.db_tablespace = \"tbl_tbsp\"` places its table in `tbl_tbsp`. `Meta.db_table` points it at the reference model\u2019s physical table, and `managed = False` normally prevents migrations from trying to create it because the test database may not contain those tablespaces.\n\n- Index configuration: `code` explicitly uses `db_tablespace=\"idx_tbsp\"`, while `title` has no explicit index tablespace. `Field.db_tablespace` falls back to `settings.DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE` in [django/db/models/fields/__init__.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:961). For generated index SQL, `_get_index_tablespace_sql()` applies this precedence:\n  1. Explicit index tablespace.\n  2. A single field\u2019s tablespace.\n  3. `DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE`.\n  4. The model\u2019s `db_tablespace`.\n  \n  This is implemented in [django/db/backends/base/schema.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/backends/base/schema.py:1541).\n\n- Many-to-many configuration: auto-created through models inherit `Article._meta.db_tablespace`, so both join tables use `tbl_tbsp`. Their foreign-key indexes inherit the individual `ManyToManyField.db_tablespace`: `authors` therefore falls back to the default/model tablespace, while `reviewers` uses `idx_tbsp`. This propagation occurs in `create_many_to_many_intermediary_model()` in [django/db/models/fields/related.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/models/fields/related.py:1400).\n\n- Database routing and backend capability: migration operations first call `Options.can_migrate()`, which rejects unmanaged models, and only then call `router.allow_migrate_model()`; see [django/db/migrations/operations/base.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/migrations/operations/base.py:148) and [django/db/models/options.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/models/options.py:395). Thus, `managed=False` prevents routers and migrations from creating `Article` under normal test-suite migration runs. The tablespace tests temporarily set `managed=True` to collect schema SQL.\n\nActual SQL ultimately depends on `connection.features.supports_tablespaces` and `connection.ops.tablespace_sql()`. PostgreSQL and Oracle set the feature to `True` and emit `TABLESPACE ...` or inline `USING INDEX TABLESPACE ...`; the base backend defaults to `False` and returns empty tablespace SQL. Consequently, unsupported backends silently ignore all of `Article`\u2019s tablespace choices, as verified in [tests/model_options/test_tablespaces.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/tests/model_options/test_tablespaces.py:58). Django also assumes the named tablespaces already exist\u2014it does not provision them for this model.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 9, "relevance": 9, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 37164, "output_tokens": 1753, "total_tokens": 38917, "cache_read_tokens": 124160, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 5, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["django\\\\db\\\\backends\\\\base\\\\features.py", "django\\\\db\\\\backends\\\\base\\\\operations.py", "django\\\\db\\\\backends\\\\base\\\\schema.py", "django\\\\db\\\\backends\\\\oracle\\\\features.py", "django\\\\db\\\\backends\\\\oracle\\\\operations.py", "django\\\\db\\\\backends\\\\postgresql\\\\features.py", "django\\\\db\\\\backends\\\\postgresql\\\\operations.py", "django\\\\db\\\\migrations\\\\operations\\\\base.py", "django\\\\db\\\\models\\\\fields\\\\__init__.py", "django\\\\db\\\\models\\\\fields\\\\related.py", "django\\\\db\\\\models\\\\options.py", "django\\\\db\\\\utils.py", "features.py", "tests\\\\model_options\\\\models\\\\tablespaces.py", "tests\\\\model_options\\\\test_tablespaces.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "code-review-graph", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "code-review-graph", "server_name": "crg", "launch_command": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/code-review-graph.exe", "launch_args": ["serve", "--repo", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django"], "served_tools": null, "client_tools": ["mcp__crg__semantic_search_nodes_tool", "mcp__crg__query_graph_tool", "mcp__crg__traverse_graph_tool", "mcp__crg__get_flow_tool", "mcp__crg__list_flows_tool", "mcp__crg__get_affected_flows_tool", "mcp__crg__get_architecture_overview_tool", "mcp__crg__get_bridge_nodes_tool", "mcp__crg__get_community_tool", "mcp__crg__list_communities_tool", "mcp__crg__get_hub_nodes_tool", "mcp__crg__get_impact_radius_tool", "mcp__crg__get_knowledge_gaps_tool", "mcp__crg__get_minimal_context_tool", "mcp__crg__get_docs_section_tool", "mcp__crg__get_wiki_page_tool", "mcp__crg__get_suggested_questions_tool", "mcp__crg__get_surprising_connections_tool", "mcp__crg__find_large_functions_tool", "mcp__crg__list_graph_stats_tool"], "index": {"command": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/code-review-graph.exe", "build", "--repo", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django", "--embedding-provider", "local", "--embedding-model", "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2"], "timeout_seconds": 10800}, "shares_index_with": null, "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django"}, "served_tools": ["apply_refactor_tool", "build_or_update_graph_tool", "cross_repo_search_tool", "detect_changes_tool", "embed_graph_tool", "find_large_functions_tool", "generate_wiki_tool", "get_affected_flows_tool", "get_architecture_overview_tool", "get_bridge_nodes_tool", "get_community_tool", "get_docs_section_tool", "get_flow_tool", "get_hub_nodes_tool", "get_impact_radius_tool", "get_knowledge_gaps_tool", "get_minimal_context_tool", "get_review_context_tool", "get_suggested_questions_tool", "get_surprising_connections_tool", "get_wiki_page_tool", "list_communities_tool", "list_flows_tool", "list_graph_stats_tool", "list_repos_tool", "query_graph_tool", "refactor_tool", "run_postprocess_tool", "semantic_search_nodes_tool", "traverse_graph_tool"], "served_count": 30, "mcp_tools_issued": ["mcp__crg__semantic_search_nodes_tool"], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": true, "mcp_per_server": {"crg": {"ok": 1, "error": 0}}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {"arm": "code-review-graph", "rc": 0, "seconds": 160.3, "argv": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/code-review-graph.exe", "build", "--repo", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django", "--embedding-provider", "local", "--embedding-model", "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2"], "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django"}, "models_used": ["gpt-5.6-sol"], "prompt_style": "neutral", "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "wall_clock_seconds": 80.44153952598572, "index_time_seconds": 160.3, "judge_time_seconds": 4.293959379196167, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.079505, "error": null, "timed_out": false, "retries": 0, "timestamp": "2026-08-05T13:46:37.083681+00:00", "prompt_sent": "Answer the following question about this code repository.\nBe specific and reference actual code files and functions.\n\nQUESTION: What are the tablespace configuration dependencies of the Article class that interact with Django's database routing and the underlying database system's tablespace management capabilities?\n\nThink step by step. Use the available tools to explore the codebase.", "model_used": "gpt-5.6-sol", "session_id": "", "stop_reason": "", "duration_api_ms": 80439, "repo_commit": "3b161e60964a", "raw_output_file": "logs\\layerb_codex_bakeoff_django\\raw_outputs\\django_000_code-review-graph.json"}
{"task_id": "django_000", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "serena", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "The tablespace behavior of `Article` depends on three layers: model metadata, database routing/migration eligibility, and backend tablespace support.\n\n- In [tests/model_options/models/tablespaces.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/tests/model_options/models/tablespaces.py:33), `Article` declares:\n\n  - `Meta.db_tablespace = \"tbl_tbsp\"` for the article table.\n  - `code(..., unique=True, db_tablespace=\"idx_tbsp\")`, placing its implicit unique index in `idx_tbsp`.\n  - `title(..., unique=True)` with no explicit field tablespace, so it falls back through the index/model defaults.\n  - `authors`, whose generated join table inherits `Article`\u2019s `tbl_tbsp`.\n  - `reviewers(..., db_tablespace=\"idx_tbsp\")`, whose generated join table still inherits `tbl_tbsp`, while its foreign-key indexes use `idx_tbsp`.\n  - `managed = False`, preventing normal migration/database creation.\n\n- Global configuration participates at model-class construction time:\n\n  - `Options.__init__()` initializes `db_tablespace` from `settings.DEFAULT_TABLESPACE` in [django/db/models/options.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/models/options.py:139).\n  - `Field.db_tablespace` resolves an absent field value through `settings.DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE` in [django/db/models/fields/__init__.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:960).\n  - Both defaults are empty strings by default in [django/conf/global_settings.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/conf/global_settings.py:434).\n  - These settings are evaluated when the model is defined, which is why the tablespace tests note that later `override_settings()` calls cannot change this model\u2019s resolved configuration.\n\n- Database routing controls whether this configuration ever reaches schema creation:\n\n  - `Options.can_migrate()` returns `False` for unmanaged models in [django/db/models/options.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/models/options.py:394).\n  - Migration operations first call `can_migrate()` and then `router.allow_migrate_model()` in [django/db/migrations/operations/base.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/migrations/operations/base.py:147).\n  - The router passes the database alias, app label, model name, and model object to configured routers in [django/db/utils.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/utils.py:270).\n\n  Thus, `Article`\u2019s normal `managed=False` status blocks migration before router approval can create its tables. The tests temporarily set `Article`, `Scientist`, and their generated through models to managed so schema SQL can be examined.\n\n- The generated many-to-many models depend directly on `Article`:\n\n  - `create_many_to_many_intermediary_model()` copies `klass._meta.db_tablespace` into each through model and copies the M2M field\u2019s `db_tablespace` onto its two foreign keys in [django/db/models/fields/related.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/models/fields/related.py:1395).\n  - Consequently, both join tables use `tbl_tbsp`; only the `reviewers` join-table indexes explicitly use `idx_tbsp`.\n\n- Actual enforcement is delegated to the selected database backend:\n\n  - Base backends advertise `supports_tablespaces = False` in [django/db/backends/base/features.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/backends/base/features.py:125).\n  - Schema creation asks `connection.ops.tablespace_sql()` for table placement and only emits inline unique-index placement when `connection.features.supports_tablespaces` is true in [django/db/backends/base/schema.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/backends/base/schema.py:301).\n  - Unsupported backends return no tablespace SQL, making `Article` equivalent to the reference model for schema-generation purposes.\n  - PostgreSQL and Oracle set `supports_tablespaces = True` and implement `tablespace_sql()` as `TABLESPACE ...` or, for inline indexes, `USING INDEX TABLESPACE ...` in [django/db/backends/postgresql/operations.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/backends/postgresql/operations.py:234) and [django/db/backends/oracle/operations.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/backends/oracle/operations.py:572).\n\nIn short: routing and `managed` status decide whether `Article` may be created on a given connection; model/field/default settings decide the requested tablespaces; and the routed connection\u2019s backend features and operations decide whether those requests become real database-specific SQL or are silently ignored.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 10, "relevance": 10, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 44185, "output_tokens": 2086, "total_tokens": 46271, "cache_read_tokens": 195840, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 19, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": [], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "serena", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "serena", "server_name": "serena", "launch_command": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/serena.exe", "launch_args": ["start-mcp-server", "--project", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-serena-django-django", "--transport", "stdio", "--enable-web-dashboard", "false", "--enable-gui-log-window", "false"], "served_tools": null, "client_tools": ["mcp__serena__search_for_pattern", "mcp__serena__find_symbol", "mcp__serena__get_symbols_overview", "mcp__serena__find_declaration", "mcp__serena__find_implementations", "mcp__serena__find_referencing_symbols", "mcp__serena__get_diagnostics_for_file", "mcp__serena__find_file", "mcp__serena__list_dir", "mcp__serena__read_file"], "index": null, "shares_index_with": null, "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-serena-django-django"}, "served_tools": ["activate_project", "create_text_file", "delete_memory", "edit_memory", "execute_shell_command", "find_declaration", "find_file", "find_implementations", "find_referencing_symbols", "find_symbol", "get_current_config", "get_diagnostics_for_file", "get_symbols_overview", "initial_instructions", "insert_after_symbol", "insert_before_symbol", "list_dir", "list_memories", "onboarding", "read_file", "read_memory", "rename_memory", "rename_symbol", "replace_content", "replace_in_files", "replace_symbol_body", "safe_delete_symbol", "search_for_pattern", "write_memory"], "served_count": 29, "mcp_tools_issued": ["mcp__serena__initial_instructions", "mcp__serena__activate_project", "mcp__serena__search_for_pattern", "mcp__serena__find_symbol", "mcp__serena__read_file", "mcp__serena__read_file", "mcp__serena__read_file", "mcp__serena__read_file", "mcp__serena__search_for_pattern", "mcp__serena__read_file", "mcp__serena__read_file", "mcp__serena__read_file", "mcp__serena__read_file", "mcp__serena__read_file", "mcp__serena__read_file", "mcp__serena__read_file", "mcp__serena__read_file", "mcp__serena__read_file", "mcp__serena__read_file"], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": true, "mcp_per_server": {"serena": {"ok": 19, "error": 0}}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {"skipped": "no-index-by-design", "seconds": 0.0}, "models_used": ["gpt-5.6-sol"], "prompt_style": "neutral", "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "wall_clock_seconds": 83.22959423065186, "index_time_seconds": 0.0, "judge_time_seconds": 5.491847515106201, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.10057125, "error": null, "timed_out": false, "retries": 0, "timestamp": "2026-08-05T13:50:59.146504+00:00", "prompt_sent": "Answer the following question about this code repository.\nBe specific and reference actual code files and functions.\n\nQUESTION: What are the tablespace configuration dependencies of the Article class that interact with Django's database routing and the underlying database system's tablespace management capabilities?\n\nThink step by step. Use the available tools to explore the codebase.", "model_used": "gpt-5.6-sol", "session_id": "", "stop_reason": "", "duration_api_ms": 83227, "repo_commit": "3b161e60964a", "raw_output_file": "logs\\layerb_codex_bakeoff_django\\raw_outputs\\django_000_serena.json"}
{"task_id": "django_004", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "c0-bare", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "`DetailViewTest` uses an **orthogonality/invariant-testing pattern**: it varies the object lookup strategy while repeatedly asserting that context naming and template selection remain unchanged.\n\nSpecifically:\n\n- The URL configuration supplies several lookup variants\u2014standard/custom PK, standard/custom slug, PK with an ignored slug, and combined PK-and-slug filtering\u2014in [tests/generic_views/urls.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/tests/generic_views/urls.py:39).\n- Tests such as `test_detail_by_pk()`, `test_detail_by_custom_pk()`, `test_detail_by_slug()`, and `test_detail_by_custom_slug()` then assert the same downstream invariants: both `\"object\"` and the model-derived `\"author\"` context variables contain the resolved `Author`, and `generic_views/author_detail.html` is selected ([test_detail.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/tests/generic_views/test_detail.py:44)).\n- Separate tests alter only one presentation concern at a time: `context_object_name`, `template_name`, `template_name_suffix`, or `template_name_field`, confirming that each customization operates independently of lookup ([test_detail.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/tests/generic_views/test_detail.py:130)).\n- `test_custom_detail()` is the strongest isolation check. `AuthorCustomDetail.get()` bypasses the normal `BaseDetailView.get()` flow and passes the locally retrieved object directly to `get_context_object_name(author)`, proving naming depends on the supplied object rather than incidental `self.object` state ([views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/tests/generic_views/views.py:34)).\n- The deferred-queryset tests additionally verify that lazy/deferred field loading does not affect model-derived context or template names ([test_detail.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/tests/generic_views/test_detail.py:184)).\n\nThis mirrors the production separation of concerns: `SingleObjectMixin.get_object()` performs lookup, `get_context_object_name(obj)` derives naming from the resolved object, and `SingleObjectTemplateResponseMixin.get_template_names()` resolves templates from the object/model metadata ([detail.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/views/generic/detail.py:19)). Thus, the suite treats lookup as a replaceable strategy and context/template behavior as invariant downstream policies.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 9, "relevance": 9, "clarity": 8, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 12022, "output_tokens": 1145, "total_tokens": 13167, "cache_read_tokens": 77568, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 4, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": [".\\\\django\\\\views\\\\generic\\\\detail.py", ".\\\\tests\\\\generic_views\\\\models.py", ".\\\\tests\\\\generic_views\\\\test_detail.py", ".\\\\tests\\\\generic_views\\\\urls.py", ".\\\\tests\\\\generic_views\\\\views.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "c0-bare", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "c0-bare", "server_name": null, "launch_command": null, "launch_args": null, "served_tools": null, "client_tools": [], "index": null, "shares_index_with": null, "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-c0-bare-django-django"}, "served_tools": [], "served_count": null, "mcp_tools_issued": [], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": null, "mcp_per_server": {}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {}, "models_used": ["gpt-5.6-sol"], "prompt_style": "neutral", "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "wall_clock_seconds": 56.2648606300354, "index_time_seconds": 0.0, "judge_time_seconds": 4.434523820877075, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.0361735, "error": null, "timed_out": false, "retries": 0, "timestamp": "2026-08-05T13:52:37.707957+00:00", "prompt_sent": "Answer the following question about this code repository.\nBe specific and reference actual code files and functions.\n\nQUESTION: What architectural pattern does DetailViewTest employ to verify that context object naming and template resolution mechanisms maintain independence from the underlying object lookup strategy?\n\nThink step by step. Use the available tools to explore the codebase.", "model_used": "gpt-5.6-sol", "session_id": "", "stop_reason": "", "duration_api_ms": 56263, "repo_commit": "3b161e60964a", "raw_output_file": "logs\\layerb_codex_bakeoff_django\\raw_outputs\\django_004_c0-bare.json"}
{"task_id": "django_004", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "repowise", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "`DetailViewTest` uses a strategy-invariance testing pattern built on Django\u2019s mixin-based separation of concerns.\n\nIt varies the object lookup strategy while repeatedly asserting the same downstream invariants:\n\n- Primary-key, custom-primary-key, slug, custom-slug, and combined PK/slug lookups all produce the same `object` and model-derived `author` context keys and resolve `generic_views/author_detail.html` ([test_detail.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/tests/generic_views/test_detail.py:46)).\n- Deferred-field lookup is tested separately to confirm that loading an `Author` through `Author.objects.defer(...)` does not alter template derivation or context naming ([test_detail.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/tests/generic_views/test_detail.py:185)).\n- `AuthorCustomDetail.get()` deliberately bypasses the normal `BaseDetailView.get()` context flow and passes a locally retrieved object directly to `get_context_object_name(author)`, proving naming depends on the supplied object rather than `self.object` ([views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/tests/generic_views/views.py:35)).\n\nThis works because production responsibilities are orthogonal:\n\n- `SingleObjectMixin.get_object()` encapsulates lookup.\n- `get_context_object_name(obj)` derives the name from the resulting object.\n- `SingleObjectTemplateResponseMixin.get_template_names()` derives templates from the resulting object/model metadata.\n- `DetailView` composes those behaviors through multiple mixins ([detail.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/django/views/generic/detail.py:8)).\n\nSo, architecturally, it is a combination of the Strategy pattern and mixin-based separation of concerns, verified through parameter-like behavioral/contract tests: change the retrieval strategy, then assert that context naming and template resolution remain invariant.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 9, "relevance": 10, "clarity": 8, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 28735, "output_tokens": 975, "total_tokens": 29710, "cache_read_tokens": 108288, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 3, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["django/views/generic/detail.py", "tests/generic_views/views.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": ["mcp__repowise__get_answer"], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "repowise", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "repowise", "server_name": "repowise", "launch_command": "C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/repowise-layerb/.venv/Scripts/repowise.exe", "launch_args": ["mcp", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-repowise-full-django-django", "--transport", "stdio"], "served_tools": null, "client_tools": ["mcp__repowise__get_answer", "mcp__repowise__get_context", "mcp__repowise__get_overview", "mcp__repowise__get_risk", "mcp__repowise__get_symbol", "mcp__repowise__get_why", "mcp__repowise__search_codebase"], "index": null, "shares_index_with": "repowise-full", "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-repowise-full-django-django"}, "served_tools": ["get_answer", "get_change_risk", "get_context", "get_dead_code", "get_health", "get_overview", "get_risk", "get_symbol", "get_why", "list_repos", "search_codebase"], "served_count": 11, "mcp_tools_issued": ["mcp__repowise__get_answer"], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": true, "mcp_per_server": {"repowise": {"ok": 1, "error": 0}}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {"builtin": "repowise_legacy", "rc": 0, "seconds": 0.0, "index_vector_dim": 1536, "index_embedder_mock": false}, "models_used": ["gpt-5.6-sol"], "prompt_style": "neutral", "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "wall_clock_seconds": 43.77914357185364, "index_time_seconds": 0.0, "judge_time_seconds": 5.445945739746094, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.05920475, "error": null, "timed_out": false, "retries": 0, "timestamp": "2026-08-05T13:53:38.562093+00:00", "prompt_sent": "Answer the following question about this code repository.\nBe specific and reference actual code files and functions.\n\nQUESTION: What architectural pattern does DetailViewTest employ to verify that context object naming and template resolution mechanisms maintain independence from the underlying object lookup strategy?\n\nThink step by step. Use the available tools to explore the codebase.", "model_used": "gpt-5.6-sol", "session_id": "", "stop_reason": "", "duration_api_ms": 43777, "repo_commit": "3b161e60964a", "raw_output_file": "logs\\layerb_codex_bakeoff_django\\raw_outputs\\django_004_repowise.json"}
{"task_id": "django_004", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "codegraph", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "`DetailViewTest` uses a contract-testing pattern across interchangeable lookup strategies.\n\nThe tests retrieve the same `Author` through several mechanisms:\n\n- Default and custom primary-key arguments\n- Default and custom slug arguments\n- Primary key with an ignored slug\n- Combined primary-key-and-slug lookup\n\nDespite changing lookup configuration in [tests/generic_views/urls.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/tests/generic_views/urls.py:38), each successful case in [tests/generic_views/test_detail.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/tests/generic_views/test_detail.py:37) repeats the same invariant assertions:\n\n- `context[\"object\"]` contains the retrieved instance.\n- The model-derived `context[\"author\"]` contains that instance.\n- `generic_views/author_detail.html` is selected.\n\nThis verifies separation of concerns: `SingleObjectMixin.get_object()` handles lookup strategy, while `get_context_object_name()` derives the context name from the resulting object and `SingleObjectTemplateResponseMixin.get_template_names()` derives the template from its model metadata. Those downstream mechanisms consume the resolved object and do not depend on whether it came from a PK, slug, custom URL keyword, combined filter, or overridden `get()` implementation ([django/views/generic/detail.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/django/views/generic/detail.py:21), [django/views/generic/detail.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/django/views/generic/detail.py:83), [django/views/generic/detail.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/django/views/generic/detail.py:121)).\n\nThe custom-name, template-name, deferred-queryset, and `AuthorCustomDetail` cases strengthen this as orthogonality testing: each concern is varied independently while the others\u2019 contracts remain unchanged.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 9, "relevance": 10, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 26550, "output_tokens": 980, "total_tokens": 27530, "cache_read_tokens": 103936, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 4, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": [".\\\\django\\\\views\\\\generic\\\\detail.py", ".\\\\tests\\\\generic_views\\\\test_detail.py", ".\\\\tests\\\\generic_views\\\\urls.py", ".\\\\tests\\\\generic_views\\\\views.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "codegraph", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "codegraph", "server_name": "codegraph", "launch_command": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm/codegraph.cmd", "launch_args": ["serve", "--mcp", "--path", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django", "--no-watch"], "served_tools": null, "client_tools": ["mcp__codegraph__codegraph_explore"], "index": {"command": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm/codegraph.cmd", "init", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django"], "timeout_seconds": 10800}, "shares_index_with": null, "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django"}, "served_tools": ["codegraph_explore"], "served_count": 1, "mcp_tools_issued": ["mcp__codegraph__codegraph_explore"], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": true, "mcp_per_server": {"codegraph": {"ok": 1, "error": 0}}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {"arm": "codegraph", "rc": 0, "seconds": 2.6, "argv": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm/codegraph.cmd", "init", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django"], "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django"}, "models_used": 