{"task_id": "django_008", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "c0-bare", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "`assertLoginRedirectURLEqual()` has two implicit dependencies inherited through `self.login()`:\n\n1. **A working session middleware stack**\n\n   In [tests/auth_tests/test_views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:1031), the helper calls `self.login()`. That inherited method posts credentials and then requires `SESSION_KEY` to exist in `self.client.session` at line 87.\n\n   The login view calls `auth_login()` in [django/contrib/auth/views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/contrib/auth/views.py:114), which writes the user ID, backend, and authentication hash into `request.session` in [django/contrib/auth/__init__.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/contrib/auth/__init__.py:151). Therefore:\n\n   - `SessionMiddleware` must have attached `request.session`.\n   - Its response processing must save the modified session and issue/update the session cookie.\n   - The test client must retain that cookie so `self.client.session` can reload the authenticated session.\n\n   The test runner supplies this implicitly: `SessionMiddleware` is first in `ALWAYS_MIDDLEWARE` in [tests/runtests.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/tests/runtests.py:86). Without it, login would fail when accessing `request.session`, or the line-87 assertion would fail if session state were not persisted.\n\n2. **The test client\u2019s default CSRF bypass, while retaining CSRF rotation**\n\n   `self.login()` sends a raw POST containing only `username` and `password`; it performs no preliminary GET and supplies no CSRF token. However, `LoginView` is decorated with `csrf_protect` in [django/contrib/auth/views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/contrib/auth/views.py:73).\n\n   This succeeds because Django\u2019s test client defaults to `enforce_csrf_checks=False` in [django/test/client.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/test/client.py:1050). Its handler sets `request._dont_enforce_csrf_checks`, causing `CsrfViewMiddleware` to skip rejecting the tokenless POST.\n\n   Importantly, bypassing validation does **not** bypass login\u2019s CSRF-token rotation. `auth_login()` still calls `rotate_token(request)` at [django/contrib/auth/__init__.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/contrib/auth/__init__.py:180). That generates a new CSRF secret and marks it for update in [django/middleware/csrf.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/middleware/csrf.py:117); `CsrfViewMiddleware.process_response()` then persists it as a cookie, or in the session when `CSRF_USE_SESSIONS=True`.\n\nThus, the redirect helper appears to test only `LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL`, but it actually assumes that session middleware is correctly installed and ordered, that the normal test client suppresses CSRF validation for its tokenless login POST, and that the successful login can still rotate and persist the CSRF token.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 9, "relevance": 10, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 30479, "output_tokens": 2155, "total_tokens": 32634, "cache_read_tokens": 180480, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 10, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["django/contrib/auth/__init__.py", "django/contrib/auth/views.py", "django/contrib/sessions/middleware.py", "django/middleware/csrf.py", "django/test/client.py", "tests/auth_tests/settings.py", "tests/auth_tests/test_views.py", "tests/auth_tests/urls.py", "tests/runtests.py", "tests\\\\auth_tests\\\\test_views.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "c0-bare", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "c0-bare", "server_name": null, "launch_command": null, "launch_args": null, "served_tools": null, "client_tools": [], "index": null, "shares_index_with": null, "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-c0-bare-django-django"}, "served_tools": [], "served_count": null, "mcp_tools_issued": [], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": null, "mcp_per_server": {}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {}, "models_used": ["gpt-5.6-sol"], "prompt_style": "neutral", "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "wall_clock_seconds": 98.25387287139893, "index_time_seconds": 0.0, "judge_time_seconds": 7.189698696136475, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.08220875, "error": null, "timed_out": false, "retries": 0, "timestamp": "2026-08-05T14:08:03.434749+00:00", "prompt_sent": "Answer the following question about this code repository.\nBe specific and reference actual code files and functions.\n\nQUESTION: What implicit dependencies exist between the assertLoginRedirectURLEqual helper method and the self.login() method inherited from AuthViewsTestCase regarding session middleware and CSRF token handling?\n\nThink step by step. Use the available tools to explore the codebase.", "model_used": "gpt-5.6-sol", "session_id": "", "stop_reason": "", "duration_api_ms": 98252, "repo_commit": "3b161e60964a", "raw_output_file": "logs\\layerb_codex_bakeoff_django\\raw_outputs\\django_008_c0-bare.json"}
{"task_id": "django_008", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "repowise", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "`assertLoginRedirectURLEqual()` has two implicit environmental dependencies because it delegates the actual request to the inherited `AuthViewsTestCase.login()`:\n\n- `assertLoginRedirectURLEqual()` calls `self.login()` and then asserts that its response redirects to the configured URL ([tests/auth_tests/test_views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:1031)).\n- That `login()` is not `Client.login()`. It performs a real POST to `/login/`, then verifies that `SESSION_KEY` exists in `self.client.session` ([tests/auth_tests/test_views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:79)).\n\nThe implicit dependencies are:\n\n1. Session middleware must attach and persist `request.session`.\n\n   The login view calls `auth_login()` before constructing the redirect ([django/contrib/auth/views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/django/contrib/auth/views.py:114)). `auth_login()` cycles or flushes the session and writes the user, backend, and authentication hash into it ([django/contrib/auth/__init__.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/django/contrib/auth/__init__.py:151)). This assumes `SessionMiddleware.process_request()` has installed `request.session`, and its response processing saves that session and cookie ([django/contrib/sessions/middleware.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/django/contrib/sessions/middleware.py:12)).\n\n   Without session middleware, login fails before producing the expected redirect; without session persistence, the explicit `SESSION_KEY` assertion in `self.login()` fails.\n\n2. CSRF protection is implicitly bypassed by the default test client.\n\n   `self.login()` submits no `csrfmiddlewaretoken`, even though the login view is CSRF-protected. This works because `TestCase`\u2019s normal `Client` defaults to `enforce_csrf_checks=False` ([django/test/client.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/django/test/client.py:1048)). Its handler sets `_dont_enforce_csrf_checks`, allowing the POST through `CsrfViewMiddleware` without a token ([django/test/client.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/django/test/client.py:165)).\n\nThus, the redirect helper silently assumes a middleware-backed session and the standard CSRF-bypassing test client. Replacing the client with `Client(enforce_csrf_checks=True)` would require first obtaining a CSRF cookie and posting a matching token; otherwise the helper would receive a 403 rather than the redirect it expects.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 8, "reasoning": 9, "relevance": 9, "clarity": 9}, "input_tokens": 40609, "output_tokens": 1547, "total_tokens": 42156, "cache_read_tokens": 159744, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 5, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["django/contrib/auth/__init__.py", "django/contrib/auth/views.py", "django/contrib/sessions/middleware.py", "django/test/client.py", "tests/auth_tests/test_views.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": ["mcp__repowise__get_answer"], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "repowise", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "repowise", "server_name": "repowise", "launch_command": "C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/repowise-layerb/.venv/Scripts/repowise.exe", "launch_args": ["mcp", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-repowise-full-django-django", "--transport", "stdio"], "served_tools": null, "client_tools": ["mcp__repowise__get_answer", "mcp__repowise__get_context", "mcp__repowise__get_overview", "mcp__repowise__get_risk", "mcp__repowise__get_symbol", "mcp__repowise__get_why", "mcp__repowise__search_codebase"], "index": null, "shares_index_with": "repowise-full", "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-repowise-full-django-django"}, "served_tools": ["get_answer", "get_change_risk", "get_context", "get_dead_code", "get_health", "get_overview", "get_risk", "get_symbol", "get_why", "list_repos", "search_codebase"], "served_count": 11, "mcp_tools_issued": ["mcp__repowise__get_answer"], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": true, "mcp_per_server": {"repowise": {"ok": 1, "error": 0}}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {"builtin": "repowise_legacy", "rc": 0, "seconds": 0.0, "index_vector_dim": 1536, "index_embedder_mock": false}, "models_used": ["gpt-5.6-sol"], "prompt_style": "neutral", "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "wall_clock_seconds": 75.34926772117615, "index_time_seconds": 0.0, "judge_time_seconds": 6.030718088150024, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.08619924999999999, "error": null, "timed_out": false, "retries": 0, "timestamp": "2026-08-05T14:09:49.036547+00:00", "prompt_sent": "Answer the following question about this code repository.\nBe specific and reference actual code files and functions.\n\nQUESTION: What implicit dependencies exist between the assertLoginRedirectURLEqual helper method and the self.login() method inherited from AuthViewsTestCase regarding session middleware and CSRF token handling?\n\nThink step by step. Use the available tools to explore the codebase.", "model_used": "gpt-5.6-sol", "session_id": "", "stop_reason": "", "duration_api_ms": 75343, "repo_commit": "3b161e60964a", "raw_output_file": "logs\\layerb_codex_bakeoff_django\\raw_outputs\\django_008_repowise.json"}
{"task_id": "django_008", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "codegraph", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "`LoginRedirectUrlTest.assertLoginRedirectURLEqual()` is not a pure redirect assertion. In [tests/auth_tests/test_views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:1031), it first calls the inherited `AuthViewsTestCase.login()`, which posts credentials to `/login/`. That method then asserts that `SESSION_KEY` exists in `self.client.session` ([test_views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:79)).\n\nThis creates two implicit dependencies:\n\n- **Session middleware is required.** `LoginView.form_valid()` calls `auth_login(self.request, form.get_user())` ([django/contrib/auth/views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/django/contrib/auth/views.py:114)). `auth_login()` reads, cycles, and writes `request.session`, including `SESSION_KEY`, the backend, and the authentication hash ([django/contrib/auth/__init__.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/django/contrib/auth/__init__.py:151)). Therefore, `SessionMiddleware` must have attached a session to the request; otherwise the helper fails before it ever checks `LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL`. The auth test middleware configuration also places `SessionMiddleware` before `AuthenticationMiddleware` ([tests/auth_tests/settings.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/tests/auth_tests/settings.py:3)).\n\n- **The POST implicitly relies on the test client\u2019s CSRF bypass.** `self.login()` submits no `csrfmiddlewaretoken`, even though it posts to the login view. This succeeds because Django\u2019s default `Client` uses `enforce_csrf_checks=False` ([django/test/client.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/django/test/client.py:1048)); `ClientHandler` consequently marks the request with `_dont_enforce_csrf_checks`, bypassing `CsrfViewMiddleware` validation ([django/test/client.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/django/test/client.py:165)). If the client were replaced with `Client(enforce_csrf_checks=True)`, the helper would need to GET a token and submit both the CSRF cookie and form token.\n\nSuccessful authentication still calls `rotate_token(request)` inside `auth_login()` ([django/contrib/auth/__init__.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/django/contrib/auth/__init__.py:180)), so the CSRF secret is rotated on login even though validation was bypassed. `CsrfViewMiddleware.process_response()` writes that rotated value to the response cookie ([django/middleware/csrf.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/django/middleware/csrf.py:472)).\n\nThus, failures caused by missing session middleware or enabled CSRF enforcement can misleadingly surface through `assertLoginRedirectURLEqual()` as login/session failures rather than problems with redirect URL resolution.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 9, "relevance": 10, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 29256, "output_tokens": 1564, "total_tokens": 30820, "cache_read_tokens": 118272, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 4, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["django/contrib/auth/__init__.py", "django/contrib/auth/views.py", "django/middleware/csrf.py", "django/test/client.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "codegraph", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "codegraph", "server_name": "codegraph", "launch_command": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm/codegraph.cmd", "launch_args": ["serve", "--mcp", "--path", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django", "--no-watch"], "served_tools": null, "client_tools": ["mcp__codegraph__codegraph_explore"], "index": {"command": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm/codegraph.cmd", "init", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django"], "timeout_seconds": 10800}, "shares_index_with": null, "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django"}, "served_tools": ["codegraph_explore"], "served_count": 1, "mcp_tools_issued": ["mcp__codegraph__codegraph_explore"], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": true, "mcp_per_server": {"codegraph": {"ok": 1, "error": 0}}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {"arm": "codegraph", "rc": 0, "seconds": 2.6, "argv": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm/codegraph.cmd", "init", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django"], "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django"}, "models_used": ["gpt-5.6-sol"], "prompt_style": "neutral", "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "wall_clock_seconds": 59.444969177246094, "index_time_seconds": 0.0, "judge_time_seconds": 4.9708685874938965, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.066994, "error": null, "timed_out": false, "retries": 0, "timestamp": "2026-08-05T14:11:16.741817+00:00", "prompt_sent": "Answer the following question about this code repository.\nBe specific and reference actual code files and functions.\n\nQUESTION: What implicit dependencies exist between the assertLoginRedirectURLEqual helper method and the self.login() method inherited from AuthViewsTestCase regarding session middleware and CSRF token handling?\n\nThink step by step. Use the available tools to explore the codebase.", "model_used": "gpt-5.6-sol", "session_id": "", "stop_reason": "", "duration_api_ms": 59443, "repo_commit": "3b161e60964a", "raw_output_file": "logs\\layerb_codex_bakeoff_django\\raw_outputs\\django_008_codegraph.json"}
{"task_id": "django_008", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "graphify", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "`assertLoginRedirectURLEqual()` has two implicit dependencies inherited through `AuthViewsTestCase.login()`:\n\n- Session middleware is required. The helper calls `self.login()`, which performs a real POST to `/login/` and then verifies that `SESSION_KEY` exists in `self.client.session` ([tests/auth_tests/test_views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:79), [tests/auth_tests/test_views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:1031)). `LoginView` ultimately calls `django.contrib.auth.login()`, which accesses `request.session`, cycles its key, and stores the user, backend, and authentication hash ([django/contrib/auth/__init__.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/contrib/auth/__init__.py:151)). Thus, `SessionMiddleware` must run before authentication handling to attach and persist `request.session`. The test runner supplies it first in `ALWAYS_MIDDLEWARE` ([tests/runtests.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/tests/runtests.py:86)). Without it, the redirect assertion would never be reached successfully.\n\n- CSRF middleware may run, but the helper relies on the test client\u2019s default CSRF bypass. `self.login()` sends only `username` and `password`; it neither fetches nor submits a `csrfmiddlewaretoken`. The ordinary `Client` defaults to `enforce_csrf_checks=False` ([django/test/client.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/test/client.py:1048)), causing the request to carry `_dont_enforce_csrf_checks=True`. `CsrfViewMiddleware` accepts such a POST without validating a token, while still retaining normal cookie-related behavior ([django/middleware/csrf.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/middleware/csrf.py:428)).\n\nThere is a further subtle interaction: successful `django.contrib.auth.login()` calls `rotate_token(request)` ([django/contrib/auth/__init__.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/contrib/auth/__init__.py:180)). Therefore CSRF state can still be rotated and emitted by middleware even though validation was bypassed. The helper does not test that behavior; a separate test explicitly constructs the session and CSRF middleware flow and verifies token rotation ([tests/auth_tests/test_views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:871)).\n\nIn short: session middleware is a hard functional prerequisite, whereas the absence of an explicit CSRF token works only because the default test client disables CSRF enforcement\u2014not because the login view is CSRF-exempt.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 9, "relevance": 10, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 28002, "output_tokens": 1583, "total_tokens": 29585, "cache_read_tokens": 155904, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 5, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["django/contrib/auth/__init__.py", "django/middleware/csrf.py", "django/test/client.py", "test_sqlite.py", "tests/auth_tests/settings.py", "tests/auth_tests/test_views.py", "tests/runtests.py", "tests/test_mysql.py", "tests/test_oracle.py", "tests/test_postgresql.py", "tests/test_sqlite.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "graphify", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "graphify", "server_name": "graphify", "launch_command": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/graphify-mcp.exe", "launch_args": ["--transport", "stdio", "--graph", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-graphify-django-django/graphify-out/graph.json"], "served_tools": null, "client_tools": ["mcp__graphify__query_graph", "mcp__graphify__get_node", "mcp__graphify__get_neighbors", "mcp__graphify__shortest_path", "mcp__graphify__get_community", "mcp__graphify__god_nodes", "mcp__graphify__graph_stats"], "index": {"command": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/graphify.exe", "update", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-graphify-django-django"], "timeout_seconds": 10800}, "shares_index_with": null, "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-graphify-django-django"}, "served_tools": ["get_community", "get_neighbors", "get_node", "get_pr_impact", "god_nodes", "graph_stats", "list_prs", "query_graph", "shortest_path", "triage_prs"], "served_count": 10, "mcp_tools_issued": ["mcp__graphify__query_graph"], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": true, "mcp_per_server": {"graphify": {"ok": 1, "error": 0}}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {"arm": "graphify", "rc": 0, "seconds": 167.4, "argv": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/graphify.exe", "update", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-graphify-django-django"], "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-graphify-django-django"}, "models_used": ["gpt-5.6-sol"], "prompt_style": "neutral", "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "wall_clock_seconds": 58.18554091453552, "index_time_seconds": 0.0, "judge_time_seconds": 5.0159735679626465, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.0703205, "error": null, "timed_out": false, "retries": 0, "timestamp": "2026-08-05T14:12:21.673694+00:00", "prompt_sent": "Answer the following question about this code repository.\nBe specific and reference actual code files and functions.\n\nQUESTION: What implicit dependencies exist between the assertLoginRedirectURLEqual helper method and the self.login() method inherited from AuthViewsTestCase regarding session middleware and CSRF token handling?\n\nThink step by step. Use the available tools to explore the codebase.", "model_used": "gpt-5.6-sol", "session_id": "", "stop_reason": "", "duration_api_ms": 