{"task_id": "django_008", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "code-review-graph", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "`LoginRedirectUrlTest.assertLoginRedirectURLEqual()` has two implicit dependencies inherited through `AuthViewsTestCase.login()`:\n\n- Session middleware is required. The helper calls `self.login()`, which POSTs to `/login/` and then verifies that `SESSION_KEY` exists in `self.client.session` ([tests/auth_tests/test_views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:79), [tests/auth_tests/test_views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:1031)). `LoginView.form_valid()` invokes `auth_login()`, which expects `request.session`, cycles or flushes its key, and stores the user ID, backend, and authentication hash ([django/contrib/auth/views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/contrib/auth/views.py:114), [django/contrib/auth/__init__.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/contrib/auth/__init__.py:151)). Thus the test silently relies on `SessionMiddleware` being installed before authentication middleware, as it is in the test runner\u2019s `ALWAYS_MIDDLEWARE` configuration ([tests/runtests.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/tests/runtests.py:86)). Without it, the login request would lack `request.session`, so no redirect assertion would be reached successfully.\n\n- CSRF protection is present but implicitly bypassed by the test client. `LoginView.dispatch` is decorated with `csrf_protect` ([django/contrib/auth/views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/contrib/auth/views.py:73)), yet `AuthViewsTestCase.login()` submits no `csrfmiddlewaretoken`. This works because the ordinary `TestCase` client defaults to `enforce_csrf_checks=False`; the client sets `request._dont_enforce_csrf_checks` accordingly before middleware processing ([django/test/client.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/test/client.py:180)). With an enforcing client, `self.login()` would need to obtain and submit a valid token or its POST would receive a 403 instead of the expected redirect.\n\nThere is also a post-authentication CSRF side effect: `auth_login()` calls `rotate_token(request)` after writing the session ([django/contrib/auth/__init__.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/contrib/auth/__init__.py:180)). Therefore `assertLoginRedirectURLEqual()` indirectly exercises CSRF-secret rotation, but does not validate it. Its redirect assertion depends only on CSRF enforcement being disabled for the tokenless POST; the rotation itself occurs after successful authentication and may update the response\u2019s CSRF cookie.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 8, "completeness": 8, "relevance": 9, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 8}, "input_tokens": 39342, "output_tokens": 1516, "total_tokens": 40858, "cache_read_tokens": 118016, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 5, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["django\\\\contrib\\\\auth\\\\__init__.py", "django\\\\contrib\\\\auth\\\\views.py", "django\\\\test\\\\client.py", "tests\\\\auth_tests\\\\test_views.py", "tests\\\\runner.py", "tests\\\\runtests.py", "tests\\\\test_mysql.py", "tests\\\\test_oracle.py", "tests\\\\test_postgresql.py", "tests\\\\test_sqlite.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "code-review-graph", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "code-review-graph", "server_name": "crg", "launch_command": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/code-review-graph.exe", "launch_args": ["serve", "--repo", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django"], "served_tools": null, "client_tools": ["mcp__crg__semantic_search_nodes_tool", "mcp__crg__query_graph_tool", "mcp__crg__traverse_graph_tool", "mcp__crg__get_flow_tool", "mcp__crg__list_flows_tool", "mcp__crg__get_affected_flows_tool", "mcp__crg__get_architecture_overview_tool", "mcp__crg__get_bridge_nodes_tool", "mcp__crg__get_community_tool", "mcp__crg__list_communities_tool", "mcp__crg__get_hub_nodes_tool", "mcp__crg__get_impact_radius_tool", "mcp__crg__get_knowledge_gaps_tool", "mcp__crg__get_minimal_context_tool", "mcp__crg__get_docs_section_tool", "mcp__crg__get_wiki_page_tool", "mcp__crg__get_suggested_questions_tool", "mcp__crg__get_surprising_connections_tool", "mcp__crg__find_large_functions_tool", "mcp__crg__list_graph_stats_tool"], "index": {"command": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/code-review-graph.exe", "build", "--repo", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django", "--embedding-provider", "local", "--embedding-model", "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2"], "timeout_seconds": 10800}, "shares_index_with": null, "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django"}, "served_tools": ["apply_refactor_tool", "build_or_update_graph_tool", "cross_repo_search_tool", "detect_changes_tool", "embed_graph_tool", "find_large_functions_tool", "generate_wiki_tool", "get_affected_flows_tool", "get_architecture_overview_tool", "get_bridge_nodes_tool", "get_community_tool", "get_docs_section_tool", "get_flow_tool", "get_hub_nodes_tool", "get_impact_radius_tool", "get_knowledge_gaps_tool", "get_minimal_context_tool", "get_review_context_tool", "get_suggested_questions_tool", "get_surprising_connections_tool", "get_wiki_page_tool", "list_communities_tool", "list_flows_tool", "list_graph_stats_tool", "list_repos_tool", "query_graph_tool", "refactor_tool", "run_postprocess_tool", "semantic_search_nodes_tool", "traverse_graph_tool"], "served_count": 30, "mcp_tools_issued": ["mcp__crg__semantic_search_nodes_tool"], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": true, "mcp_per_server": {"crg": {"ok": 1, "error": 0}}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {"arm": "code-review-graph", "rc": 0, "seconds": 160.3, "argv": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/code-review-graph.exe", "build", "--repo", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django", "--embedding-provider", "local", "--embedding-model", "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2"], "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django"}, "models_used": ["gpt-5.6-sol"], "prompt_style": "neutral", "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "wall_clock_seconds": 80.34986591339111, "index_time_seconds": 0.0, "judge_time_seconds": 4.07832932472229, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.07908950000000001, "error": null, "timed_out": false, "retries": 0, "timestamp": "2026-08-05T14:13:29.681738+00:00", "prompt_sent": "Answer the following question about this code repository.\nBe specific and reference actual code files and functions.\n\nQUESTION: What implicit dependencies exist between the assertLoginRedirectURLEqual helper method and the self.login() method inherited from AuthViewsTestCase regarding session middleware and CSRF token handling?\n\nThink step by step. Use the available tools to explore the codebase.", "model_used": "gpt-5.6-sol", "session_id": "", "stop_reason": "", "duration_api_ms": 80346, "repo_commit": "3b161e60964a", "raw_output_file": "logs\\layerb_codex_bakeoff_django\\raw_outputs\\django_008_code-review-graph.json"}
{"task_id": "django_008", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "serena", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "`LoginRedirectUrlTest.assertLoginRedirectURLEqual()` has two important implicit dependencies inherited through `AuthViewsTestCase.login()`:\n\n- **Session middleware is required.** In [tests/auth_tests/test_views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:79), `login()` submits credentials to `/login/`, then asserts that `SESSION_KEY` exists in `self.client.session`. The request must therefore have `request.session`, supplied by `SessionMiddleware`. `LoginView.form_valid()` calls `auth_login()` in [django/contrib/auth/views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/contrib/auth/views.py:114), and `django.contrib.auth.login()` reads, cycles, and writes `request.session` before storing the user ID, backend, and authentication hash in [django/contrib/auth/__init__.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/contrib/auth/__init__.py:150). Without session middleware, the login POST cannot establish authentication, and the helper cannot reach its redirect assertion. `AuthenticationMiddleware` also conventionally follows `SessionMiddleware`, as shown by `AUTH_MIDDLEWARE` in [tests/auth_tests/settings.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/tests/auth_tests/settings.py:3).\n\n- **CSRF checks are implicitly bypassed by the normal test client.** `LoginView.dispatch` is explicitly wrapped with `csrf_protect` in [django/contrib/auth/views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/contrib/auth/views.py:72), but `AuthViewsTestCase.login()` posts only `username` and `password\u2014it does not first fetch a CSRF cookie or submit a `csrfmiddlewaretoken`. This works because `TestCase` uses Django\u2019s `Client`, whose `enforce_csrf_checks` default is `False` in [django/test/client.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/test/client.py:1049). Its handler sets `request._dont_enforce_csrf_checks`, allowing the protected login POST through.\n\nThere is also a post-login CSRF side effect: `django.contrib.auth.login()` calls `rotate_token(request)`. The helper does not inspect or propagate that token explicitly; the test client\u2019s cookie handling manages it. If the test used `Client(enforce_csrf_checks=True)`, `self.login()` would need a preceding GET to obtain a CSRF token and would need to include that token in the POST. Otherwise, `assertLoginRedirectURLEqual()` would receive a CSRF failure instead of the expected login redirect.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 9, "relevance": 10, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 34556, "output_tokens": 2027, "total_tokens": 36583, "cache_read_tokens": 278784, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 16, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": [], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "serena", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "serena", "server_name": "serena", "launch_command": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/serena.exe", "launch_args": ["start-mcp-server", "--project", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-serena-django-django", "--transport", "stdio", "--enable-web-dashboard", "false", "--enable-gui-log-window", "false"], "served_tools": null, "client_tools": ["mcp__serena__search_for_pattern", "mcp__serena__find_symbol", "mcp__serena__get_symbols_overview", "mcp__serena__find_declaration", "mcp__serena__find_implementations", "mcp__serena__find_referencing_symbols", "mcp__serena__get_diagnostics_for_file", "mcp__serena__find_file", "mcp__serena__list_dir", "mcp__serena__read_file"], "index": null, "shares_index_with": null, "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-serena-django-django"}, "served_tools": ["activate_project", "create_text_file", "delete_memory", "edit_memory", "execute_shell_command", "find_declaration", "find_file", "find_implementations", "find_referencing_symbols", "find_symbol", "get_current_config", "get_diagnostics_for_file", "get_symbols_overview", "initial_instructions", "insert_after_symbol", "insert_before_symbol", "list_dir", "list_memories", "onboarding", "read_file", "read_memory", "rename_memory", "rename_symbol", "replace_content", "replace_in_files", "replace_symbol_body", "safe_delete_symbol", "search_for_pattern", "write_memory"], "served_count": 29, "mcp_tools_issued": ["mcp__serena__initial_instructions", "mcp__serena__search_for_pattern", "mcp__serena__find_symbol", "mcp__serena__find_symbol", "mcp__serena__search_for_pattern", "mcp__serena__search_for_pattern", "mcp__serena__read_file", "mcp__serena__read_file", "mcp__serena__search_for_pattern", "mcp__serena__search_for_pattern", "mcp__serena__find_symbol", "mcp__serena__find_symbol", "mcp__serena__find_symbol", "mcp__serena__search_for_pattern", "mcp__serena__find_symbol", "mcp__serena__read_file"], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": true, "mcp_per_server": {"serena": {"ok": 16, "error": 0}}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {"skipped": "no-index-by-design", "seconds": 0.0}, "models_used": ["gpt-5.6-sol"], "prompt_style": "neutral", "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "wall_clock_seconds": 84.8259494304657, "index_time_seconds": 0.0, "judge_time_seconds": 4.863818168640137, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.098313, "error": null, "timed_out": false, "retries": 0, "timestamp": "2026-08-05T14:15:13.120733+00:00", "prompt_sent": "Answer the following question about this code repository.\nBe specific and reference actual code files and functions.\n\nQUESTION: What implicit dependencies exist between the assertLoginRedirectURLEqual helper method and the self.login() method inherited from AuthViewsTestCase regarding session middleware and CSRF token handling?\n\nThink step by step. Use the available tools to explore the codebase.", "model_used": "gpt-5.6-sol", "session_id": "", "stop_reason": "", "duration_api_ms": 84822, "repo_commit": "3b161e60964a", "raw_output_file": "logs\\layerb_codex_bakeoff_django\\raw_outputs\\django_008_serena.json"}
{"task_id": "django_011", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "c0-bare", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "`test_named` depends on a specific redirect-resolution chain:\n\n1. [`LoginRedirectUrlTest.test_named`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:1043) temporarily sets `LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL` to `\"password_reset\"` and invokes the shared `assertLoginRedirectURLEqual()` helper.\n\n2. The helper logs in through [`AuthViewsTestCase.login()`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:79). After successful authentication, `LoginView.form_valid()` returns a redirect to `self.get_success_url()` in [`django/contrib/auth/views.py`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/contrib/auth/views.py:114).\n\n3. With no `next` parameter, [`LoginView.get_default_redirect_url()`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/contrib/auth/views.py:99) passes `settings.LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL` to `resolve_url()`.\n\n4. [`resolve_url()`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/shortcuts.py:164) must call `django.urls.reverse(\"password_reset\", args=[], kwargs={})`. Unlike the other tests\u2019 literal URLs, `\"password_reset\"` contains neither `/` nor `.`, so if `reverse()` raises `NoReverseMatch`, `resolve_url()` re-raises it rather than treating the value as a literal URL.\n\n5. [`django.urls.reverse()`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/urls/base.py:28) must therefore:\n\n   - Use the active `ROOT_URLCONF`, which the base test class sets to `auth_tests.urls`.\n   - Populate and query that resolver\u2019s reverse dictionary.\n   - Find the `password_reset` name imported through `django.contrib.auth.urls`.\n   - Use the pattern declared as `path(\"password_reset/\", ..., name=\"password_reset\")` in [`django/contrib/auth/urls.py`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/contrib/auth/urls.py:20).\n   - Apply the current script prefix, normally `/`, and return exactly `/password_reset/`.\n\nThe other methods expose an important asymmetry in this coupling: `test_default`, `test_custom`, and `test_remote` supply literal URLs containing `/`. For those, `reverse()` is expected to fail with `NoReverseMatch`, after which `resolve_url()` returns the original literal. For `test_named`, reversal must succeed. Thus both successful named resolution and the precise `NoReverseMatch` fallback behavior are required for all four methods to coexist correctly.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 8, "completeness": 7, "reasoning": 7, "clarity": 9, "relevance": 9}, "input_tokens": 19585, "output_tokens": 2642, "total_tokens": 22227, "cache_read_tokens": 161536, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 20, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["django\\\\contrib\\\\auth\\\\urls.py", "django\\\\contrib\\\\auth\\\\views.py", "django\\\\shortcuts.py", "django\\\\urls\\\\base.py", "django\\\\urls\\\\resolvers.py", "tests\\\\auth_tests\\\\test_views.py", "tests\\\\auth_tests\\\\urls.py", "tests\\\\test_sqlite.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "c0-bare", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "c0-bare", "server_name": null, "launch_command": null, "launch_args": null, "served_tools": null, "client_tools": [], "index": null, "shares_index_with": null, "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-c0-bare-django-django"}, "served_tools": [], "served_count": null, "mcp_tools_issued": [], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": null, "mcp_per_server": {}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {}, "models_used": ["gpt-5.6-sol"], "prompt_style": "neutral", "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "wall_clock_seconds": 93.8067238330841, "index_time_seconds": 0.0, "judge_time_seconds": 4.74619460105896, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.07109325, "error": null, "timed_out": false, "retries": 0, "timestamp": "2026-08-05T14:16:53.936173+00:00", "prompt_sent": "Answer the following question about this code repository.\nBe specific and reference actual code files and functions.\n\nQUESTION: What are the coupling dependencies between the test methods in LoginRedirectUrlTest and the django.urls.reverse function that must be satisfied for the test_named test case to pass?\n\nThink step by step. Use the available tools to explore the codebase.", "model_used": "gpt-5.6-sol", "session_id": "", "stop_reason": "", "duration_api_ms": 93805, "repo_commit": "3b161e60964a", "raw_output_file": "logs\\layerb_codex_bakeoff_django\\raw_outputs\\django_011_c0-bare.json"}
{"task_id": "django_011", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "repowise", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "`LoginRedirectUrlTest.test_named` is indirectly coupled to `django.urls.reverse()` through the configured redirect name.\n\nIn [tests/auth_tests/test_views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:1028):\n\n- `test_named` overrides `LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL` with `\"password_reset\"`.\n- Login handling must treat that value as a URL-pattern name and resolve it through `reverse()`.\n- The active URLconf must therefore contain an unnamespaced pattern named `password_reset`.\n- `reverse(\"password_reset\")` must return exactly `/password_reset/`.\n- `assertLoginRedirectURLEqual()` calls `self.login()` and verifies that the response redirects to that exact path.\n\nThus, the essential dependency chain is:\n\n```text\ntest_named\n  \u2192 LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL = \"password_reset\"\n  \u2192 reverse(\"password_reset\")\n  \u2192 \"/password_reset/\"\n  \u2192 assertRedirects(..., \"/password_reset/\")\n```\n\nThe related `RedirectURLMixinTests.test_named_urls` in the same file directly verifies that `reverse()` can resolve the authentication URL names `login`, `logout`, `password_change`, `password_change_done`, `password_reset`, `password_reset_done`, `password_reset_confirm`, and `password_reset_complete`. `password_reset_confirm` additionally requires compatible `uidb64` and `token` keyword parameters.\n\nThe other `LoginRedirectUrlTest` methods are not dependent on named reversal:\n\n- `test_default` expects `/accounts/profile/`.\n- `test_custom` supplies the literal `/custom/`.\n- `test_remote` supplies a complete remote URL.\n\nTherefore, `test_named` passes only if the `password_reset` name remains registered, accepts no arguments, and reverses to the exact path `/password_reset/`.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 8, "completeness": 6, "relevance": 9, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 7}, "input_tokens": 12083, "output_tokens": 585, "total_tokens": 12668, "cache_read_tokens": 44288, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 1, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": [], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": ["mcp__repowise__get_answer"], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "repowise", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "repowise", "server_name": "repowise", "launch_command": "C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/repowise-layerb/.venv/Scripts/repowise.exe", "launch_args": ["mcp", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-repowise-full-django-django", "--transport", "stdio"], "served_tools": null, "client_tools": ["mcp__repowise__get_answer", "mcp__repowise__get_context", "mcp__repowise__get_overview", "mcp__repowise__get_risk", "mcp__repowise__get_symbol", "mcp__repowise__get_why", "mcp__repowise__search_codebase"], "index": null, "shares_index_with": "repowise-full", "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-repowise-full-django-django"}, "served_tools": ["get_answer", "get_change_risk", "get_context", "get_dead_code", "get_health", "get_overview", "get_risk", "get_symbol", "get_why", "list_repos", "search_codebase"], "served_count": 11, "mcp_tools_issued": ["mcp__repowise__get_answer"], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": true, "mcp_per_server": {"repowise": {"ok": 1, "error": 0}}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {"builtin": "repowise_legacy", "rc": 0, "seconds": 0.0, "index_vector_dim": 1536, "index_embedder_mock": false}, "models_used": ["gpt-5.6-sol"], "prompt_style": "neutral", "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "wall_clock_seconds": 29.441173553466797, "index_time_seconds": 0.0, "judge_time_seconds": 7.916691064834595, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.026489750000000003, "error": null, "timed_out": false, "retries": 0, "timestamp": "2026-08-05T14:18:32.736404+00:00", "prompt_sent": "Answer the following question about this code repository.\nBe specific and reference actual code files and functions.\n\nQUESTION: What are the coupling dependencies between the test methods in LoginRedirectUrlTest and the django.urls.reverse function that must be satisfied for the test_named test case to pass?\n\nThink step by step. Use the available tools to explore the codebase.", "model_used": "gpt-5.6-sol", "session_id": "", "stop_reason": "", "duration_api_ms": 29439, "repo_commit": "3b161e60964a", "raw_output_file": "logs\\layerb_codex_bakeoff_django\\raw_outputs\\django_011_repowise.json"}
{"task_id": "django_011", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "codegraph", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "`LoginRedirectUrlTest.test_named` depends on this exact chain:\n\n1. `AuthViewsTestCase` supplies the test environment:\n\n   - `ROOT_URLCONF=\"auth_tests.urls\"` via `@override_settings`.\n   - `setUpTestData()` creates user `testclient` with password `password`.\n   - `login()` posts those credentials to `/login/` and verifies the session was authenticated.\n\n   See [tests/auth_tests/test_views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:59).\n\n2. `test_named()` temporarily sets `LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL` to the URL name `\"password_reset\"` and expects `/password_reset/`:\n\n   ```python\n   @override_settings(LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL=\"password_reset\")\n   def test_named(self):\n       self.assertLoginRedirectURLEqual(\"/password_reset/\")\n   ```\n\n   The shared helper performs the login and asserts the response redirects to that URL without following it. See [tests/auth_tests/test_views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:1028).\n\n3. After successful authentication, `Login.get_default_redirect_url()` passes `settings.LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL` to `resolve_url()`:\n\n   ```python\n   return resolve_url(settings.LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL)\n   ```\n\n   See [django/contrib/auth/views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/django/contrib/auth/views.py:99).\n\n4. `resolve_url(\"password_reset\")` must treat the setting as a view name and call `django.urls.reverse()`. See [django/shortcuts.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/django/shortcuts.py:164).\n\n5. `reverse()` must use the active `auth_tests.urls` resolver, find the unnamespaced name `password_reset`, and call the resolver\u2019s `_reverse_with_prefix()` with the default `/` script prefix and no arguments. See [django/urls/base.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/django/urls/base.py:28).\n\n6. The active URLconf must expose a parameterless pattern named `password_reset` whose route is `password_reset/`. That pattern ultimately comes from:\n\n   ```python\n   path(\"password_reset/\", views.PasswordResetView.as_view(), name=\"password_reset\")\n   ```\n\n   See [django/contrib/auth/urls.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-codegraph-django-django/django/contrib/auth/urls.py:20).\n\nThus, the essential coupling is:\n\n```text\ntest_named setting\n    \u2192 Login.get_default_redirect_url()\n    \u2192 resolve_url(\"password_reset\")\n    \u2192 reverse(\"password_reset\")\n    \u2192 active ROOT_URLCONF\u2019s named pattern\n    \u2192 \"/password_reset/\"\n    \u2192 assertRedirects()\n```\n\nThe other test methods constrain the same helper\u2019s broader contract: `test_default` checks the default path, `test_custom` checks a literal local path, and `test_remote` checks an absolute URL. For `test_named` specifically, `\"password_reset\"` must remain a valid reversible name mapping to exactly `/password_reset/`; renaming, namespacing, parameterizing, removing, or changing that route would break the test.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 8, "relevance": 10, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 45184, "output_tokens": 1657, "total_tokens": 46841, "cache_read_tokens": 192512, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 6, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["django/contrib/auth/urls.py", "django/shortcuts.py", "tests/auth_tests/test_views.py", "tests/auth_tests/urls.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "codegraph", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "codegraph", "server_name": "codegraph", "launch_command": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm/codegraph.cmd", "launch_args": ["serve", "--mcp", "--path", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django", "--no-watch"], "served_tools": null, "client_tools": ["mcp__codegraph__codegraph_explore"], "index": {"command": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm/codegraph.cmd", "init", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django"], "timeout_seconds": 10800}, "shares_index_with": null, "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django"}, "served_tools": ["codegraph_explore"], "served_count": 1, "mcp_tools_issued": ["mcp__codegraph__codegraph_explore", "mcp__codegraph__codegraph_explore"], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": true, "mcp_per_server": {"codegraph": {"ok": 2, "error": 0}}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {"arm": "codegraph", "rc": 0, "seconds": 1.1, "argv": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm/codegraph.cmd", "init", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django"], "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-codegraph-django-django"}, "models_used": ["gpt-5.6-sol"], "prompt_style": "neutral", "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "wall_clock_seconds": 76.63834118843079, "index_time_seconds": 1.1, "judge_time_seconds": 7.993024110794067, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.097114, "error": null, "timed_out": false, "retries": 0, "timestamp": "2026-08-05T14:20:31.063238+00:00", "prompt_sent": "Answer the following question about this code repository.\nBe specific and reference actual code files and functions.\n\nQUESTION: What are the coupling dependencies between the test methods in LoginRedirectUrlTest and the django.urls.reverse function that must be satisfied for the test_named test case to pass?\n\nThink step by step. Use the available tools to explore the codebase.", "model_used": "gpt-5.6-sol", "session_id": "", "stop_reason": "", "duration_api_ms": 76634, "repo_commit": "3b161e60964a", "raw_output_file": "logs\\layerb_codex_bakeoff_django\\raw_outputs\\django_011_codegraph.json"}
{"task_id": "django_011", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "graphify", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "`test_named` depends on this call chain:\n\n1. In [tests/auth_tests/test_views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:1042), `@override_settings` temporarily sets:\n\n   ```python\n   LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL = \"password_reset\"\n   ```\n\n2. `test_named()` calls `assertLoginRedirectURLEqual(\"/password_reset/\")`.\n\n3. That helper calls the inherited `AuthViewsTestCase.login()`, which posts valid credentials to `/login/`. The base class must have created the `testclient` user, and authentication must succeed, as verified by the session assertion in [test_views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:65).\n\n4. A successful login reaches `LoginView.form_valid()`, which calls `get_success_url()`. With no `next` parameter and no view-level `next_page`, `LoginView.get_default_redirect_url()` calls:\n\n   ```python\n   resolve_url(settings.LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL)\n   ```\n\n   in [django/contrib/auth/views.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/contrib/auth/views.py:99).\n\n5. Because `\"password_reset\"` is a bare name, `resolve_url()` must delegate to:\n\n   ```python\n   reverse(\"password_reset\")\n   ```\n\n   in [django/shortcuts.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/shortcuts.py:164). A `NoReverseMatch` cannot be treated as a literal URL here because the value contains neither `/` nor `.`.\n\n6. `reverse()` in [django/urls/base.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/urls/base.py:28) must use the active root URLconf and find the named, argument-free pattern. `AuthViewsTestCase` sets `ROOT_URLCONF=\"auth_tests.urls\"`, whose patterns include `django.contrib.auth.urls`; that module defines:\n\n   ```python\n   path(\"password_reset/\", ..., name=\"password_reset\")\n   ```\n\n   at [django/contrib/auth/urls.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/contrib/auth/urls.py:20).\n\nTherefore, the essential coupling is:\n\n```text\ntest_named\n\u2192 overridden LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL\n\u2192 shared assertion/login helpers\n\u2192 LoginView.get_default_redirect_url\n\u2192 resolve_url\n\u2192 django.urls.reverse(\"password_reset\")\n\u2192 active auth URL pattern\n\u2192 \"/password_reset/\"\n```\n\n`test_named` passes only if authentication succeeds, no higher-priority redirect target is supplied, the active URLconf exposes the exact `password_reset` name without required arguments or an incompatible namespace, and `reverse()` produces `/password_reset/`, matching the helper\u2019s redirect assertion.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 9, "relevance": 10, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 24529, "output_tokens": 1389, "total_tokens": 25918, "cache_read_tokens": 140544, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 5, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["django/contrib/auth/urls.py", "django/contrib/auth/views.py", "django/shortcuts.py", "django/urls/base.py", "tests/auth_tests/test_views.py", "tests/auth_tests/urls.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "graphify", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "graphify", "server_name": "graphify", "launch_command": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/graphify-mcp.exe", "launch_args": ["--transport", "stdio", "--graph", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-graphify-django-django/graphify-out/graph.json"], "served_tools": null, "client_tools": ["mcp__graphify__query_graph", "mcp__graphify__get_node", "mcp__graphify__get_neighbors", "mcp__graphify__shortest_path", "mcp__graphify__get_community", "mcp__graphify__god_nodes", "mcp__graphify__graph_stats"], "index":