{"task_id": "django_011", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "code-review-graph", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "For `LoginRedirectUrlTest.test_named()` to pass, these dependencies must align:\n\n1. `test_named()` temporarily sets `LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL` to the symbolic name `\"password_reset\"` using `override_settings`, then expects `/password_reset/` ([tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:1042](C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django\\tests\\auth_tests\\test_views.py:1042)).\n\n2. `assertLoginRedirectURLEqual()` calls the inherited `AuthViewsTestCase.login()`, which posts valid credentials to `/login/`, verifies that authentication created a session, and returns the response ([tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:79](C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django\\tests\\auth_tests\\test_views.py:79), [tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:1031](C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django\\tests\\auth_tests\\test_views.py:1031)).\n\n3. The test class\u2019s `ROOT_URLCONF` is `auth_tests.urls`. That URLconf prepends `django.contrib.auth.urls.urlpatterns`, so it must expose both the `/login/` endpoint and the named `password_reset` pattern ([tests/auth_tests/test_views.py:59](C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django\\tests\\auth_tests\\test_views.py:59), [tests/auth_tests/urls.py:134](C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django\\tests\\auth_tests\\urls.py:134)).\n\n4. After successful authentication, `LoginView.form_valid()` calls `get_success_url()`. With no `next` parameter, this reaches `LoginView.get_default_redirect_url()`, which passes `settings.LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL` to `resolve_url()` ([django/contrib/auth/views.py:99](C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django\\django\\contrib\\auth\\views.py:99), [django/contrib/auth/views.py:114](C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django\\django\\contrib\\auth\\views.py:114)).\n\n5. `resolve_url(\"password_reset\")` must treat the setting as a view name and call `django.urls.reverse(\"password_reset\")`. Because the value contains neither `/` nor `.`, a `NoReverseMatch` is re-raised rather than treating it as a literal URL ([django/shortcuts.py:164](C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django\\django\\shortcuts.py:164)).\n\n6. `reverse()` must use the active `auth_tests.urls` resolver and find the auth pattern declared as:\n   `path(\"password_reset/\", ..., name=\"password_reset\")`\n   ([django/contrib/auth/urls.py:20](C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django\\django\\contrib\\auth\\urls.py:20), [django/urls/base.py:28](C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django\\django\\urls\\base.py:28)).\n\nThus the critical coupling is:\n\n`test_named` \u2192 overridden setting \u2192 successful `/login/` POST \u2192 `LoginView.get_success_url()` \u2192 `resolve_url()` \u2192 `django.urls.reverse()` \u2192 named `password_reset` URL pattern \u2192 `/password_reset/`.\n\nThe test fails if authentication fails, a `next` value overrides the default, the test URLconf omits or namespaces the auth patterns differently, the pattern name changes, or `reverse()` no longer returns `/password_reset/`.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 8, "relevance": 10, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 34970, "output_tokens": 1743, "total_tokens": 36713, "cache_read_tokens": 190208, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 7, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["django/contrib/auth/views.py", "django/shortcuts.py", "django/urls/base.py", "tests/auth_tests/urls.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "code-review-graph", "a