ion features that determine whether native duration field support exists, and how does DurationField resolve database-specific duration storage implementations across different backends?\n\nThink step by step. Use the available tools to explore the codebase.", "model_used": "gpt-5.6-sol", "session_id": "", "stop_reason": "", "duration_api_ms": 67311, "repo_commit": "3b161e60964a", "raw_output_file": "logs\\layerb_codex_bakeoff_django\\raw_outputs\\django_044_codegraph.json"}
{"task_id": "django_044", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "graphify", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "Native-duration support is exposed through `connection.features`:\n\n- [`django/db/backends/base/features.py:85`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/backends/base/features.py:85) defaults `BaseDatabaseFeatures.has_native_duration_field` to `False`.\n- PostgreSQL overrides it to `True` in [`django/db/backends/postgresql/features.py:17`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/backends/postgresql/features.py:17).\n- Oracle overrides it to `True` in [`django/db/backends/oracle/features.py:28`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/backends/oracle/features.py:28).\n- MySQL and SQLite inherit `False`.\n\nEach backend\u2019s `DatabaseWrapper.features_class` points to its `DatabaseFeatures` class, and the base wrapper creates `self.features` in [`django/db/backends/base/base.py:116`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/backends/base/base.py:116).\n\n`DurationField` resolves storage through the normal `Field` type-dispatch mechanism:\n\n1. [`DurationField.get_internal_type()`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:1943) returns `\"DurationField\"`.\n2. [`Field.db_type()`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:889) uses that string to look up `connection.data_types[\"DurationField\"]`.\n3. Backend mappings provide the actual column type:\n\n   - PostgreSQL: `interval` in [`postgresql/base.py:115`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/backends/postgresql/base.py:115)\n   - Oracle: `INTERVAL DAY(9) TO SECOND(6)` in [`oracle/base.py:135`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/backends/oracle/base.py:135)\n   - MySQL: `bigint` in [`mysql/base.py:120`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/backends/mysql/base.py:120)\n   - SQLite: `bigint` in [`sqlite3/base.py:75`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/backends/sqlite3/base.py:75)\n\nValue adaptation follows the same backend split. [`DurationField.get_db_prep_value()`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:1965) delegates to `connection.ops.adapt_durationfield_value()`:\n\n- The base implementation converts `timedelta` to integer microseconds in [`base/operations.py:590`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/backends/base/operations.py:590), which MySQL and SQLite use with their `bigint` columns.\n- PostgreSQL and Oracle override that adapter to return the duration unchanged, allowing their drivers to handle native interval values.\n\nOn reads, [`DurationField.get_db_converters()`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:1968) checks `connection.features.has_native_duration_field`. Non-native backends add [`convert_durationfield_value()`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-graphify-django-django/django/db/backends/base/operations.py:683), which converts stored microseconds back into `datetime.timedelta`; native PostgreSQL and Oracle values need no such converter.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 9, "relevance": 10, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 18313, "output_tokens": 2261, "total_tokens": 20574, "cache_read_tokens": 152320, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 7, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["django/db/backends/base/base.py", "django/db/backends/base/features.py", "django/db/backends/base/operations.py", "django/db/backends/mysql/base.py", "django/db/backends/oracle/base.py", "django/db/backends/oracle/features.py", "django/db/backends/oracle/operations.py", "django/db/backends/postgresql/base.py", "django/db/backends/postgresql/features.py", "django/db/backends/postgresql/operations.py", "django/db/backends/sqlite3/base.py", "django/db/models/fields/__init__.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "graphify", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "graphify", "server_name": "graphify", "launch_command": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/graphify-mcp.exe", "launch_args": ["--transport", "stdio", "--graph", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-graphify-django-django/graphify-out/graph.json"], "served_tools": null, "client_tools": ["mcp__graphify__query_graph", "mcp__graphify__get_node", "mcp__graphify__get_neighbors", "mcp__graphify__shortest_path", "mcp__graphify__get_community", "mcp__graphify__god_nodes", "mcp__graphify__graph_stats"], "index": {"command": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/graphify.exe", "update", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-graphify-django-django"], "timeout_seconds": 10800}, "shares_index_with": null, "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-graphify-django-django"}, "served_tools": ["get_community", "get_neighbors", "get_node", "get_pr_impact", "god_nodes", "graph_stats", "list_prs", "query_graph", "shortest_path", "triage_prs"], "served_count": 10, "mcp_tools_issued": ["mcp__graphify__query_graph"], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": true, "mcp_per_server": {"graphify": {"ok": 1, "error": 0}}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {"arm": "graphify", "rc": 0, "seconds": 211.2, "argv": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/graphify.exe", "update", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-graphify-django-django"], "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-graphify-django-django"}, "models_used": ["gpt-5.6-sol"], "prompt_style": "neutral", "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "wall_clock_seconds": 79.86399149894714, "