{"task_id": "django_044", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "code-review-graph", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "Native duration support is determined by the backend\u2019s `DatabaseFeatures.has_native_duration_field` flag:\n\n- The default is `False` in [`django/db/backends/base/features.py:85`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/backends/base/features.py:85).\n- PostgreSQL overrides it to `True` in [`django/db/backends/postgresql/features.py:17`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/backends/postgresql/features.py:17).\n- Oracle overrides it to `True` in [`django/db/backends/oracle/features.py:28`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/backends/oracle/features.py:28).\n- MySQL and SQLite do not override it, so they inherit `False`.\n\n`DurationField` resolves storage and conversion in several stages:\n\n1. `DurationField.get_internal_type()` returns `\"DurationField\"` in [`django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:1943`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:1943).\n\n2. The inherited `Field.db_type(connection)` looks that name up in `connection.data_types` in [`django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:889`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:889). Each backend\u2019s `DatabaseWrapper` supplies the concrete mapping:\n\n   - PostgreSQL: `interval` \u2014 [`postgresql/base.py:115`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/backends/postgresql/base.py:115)\n   - Oracle: `INTERVAL DAY(9) TO SECOND(6)` \u2014 [`oracle/base.py:135`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/backends/oracle/base.py:135)\n   - MySQL: `bigint` \u2014 [`mysql/base.py:120`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/backends/mysql/base.py:120)\n   - SQLite: `bigint` \u2014 [`sqlite3/base.py:75`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/backends/sqlite3/base.py:75)\n\n3. For writes, `DurationField.get_db_prep_value()` delegates to `connection.ops.adapt_durationfield_value()` at [`fields/__init__.py:1965`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:1965).\n\n   - The base implementation converts a `timedelta` to integer microseconds, supporting the `bigint` representation: [`backends/base/operations.py:590`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/backends/base/operations.py:590).\n   - PostgreSQL and Oracle override this adapter to return the `timedelta` unchanged because their drivers understand native interval values: [`postgresql/operations.py:333`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/backends/postgresql/operations.py:333), [`oracle/operations.py:613`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/backends/oracle/operations.py:613).\n\n4. For reads, `DurationField.get_db_converters()` checks `connection.features.has_native_duration_field` at [`fields/__init__.py:1968`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:1968). Non-native backends add `connection.ops.convert_durationfield_value`, which turns stored microseconds back into `datetime.timedelta` in [`backends/base/operations.py:683`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/backends/base/operations.py:683). Native backends skip that conversion because their drivers already return the proper duration object.\n\nThus, the feature class says whether storage is native, while the backend `data_types` table selects the SQL column type and backend operations handle the corresponding Python-to-database and database-to-Python representation.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 10, "relevance": 10, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 42300, "output_tokens": 2179, "total_tokens": 44479, "cache_read_tokens": 175872, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 7, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["/base.py", "/operations.py", "django/db/backends/base/base.py", "django/db/backends/base/features.py", "django/db/backends/base/operations.py", "django/db/backends/mysql/base.py", "django/db/backends/oracle/base.py", "django/db/backends/oracle/features.py", "django/db/backends/postgresql/base.py", "django/db/backends/postgresql/features.py", "django/db/backends/sqlite3/base.py", "django/db/models/fields/__init__.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "code-review-graph", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "code-review-graph", "server_name": "crg", "launch_command": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/code-review-graph.exe", "launch_args": ["serve", "--repo", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-code-review-graph-django-django"], "served_tools": null, "client_tools": ["mcp__crg__semantic_search_nodes_tool", "mcp__crg__query_graph_tool", "mcp__crg__traverse_graph_tool", "mcp__crg__get_flow_tool", "mcp__crg__list_flows_tool", "mcp__crg__get_affected_flows_tool", "mcp__crg__get_architecture_overview_tool", "mcp__crg__get_bridge_nodes_tool", "mcp__crg__get_community_tool", "mcp__crg__list_communities_tool", "mcp__crg__get_hub_nodes_tool", "mcp__crg__get_impact_radius_tool", "mcp__crg__get_knowledge_gaps_tool", "mcp__crg__get_minimal_context_tool", "mcp__crg__get_docs_section_tool", "mcp__crg__get_wiki_page_tool", "mcp__crg__get_suggested_questions_tool", "mcp__crg__get_surprising_connections_tool", "mcp__crg__find_large_functions_tool", "mcp__crg__list_graph_stats_tool"], "index": {"command": ["C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/code-re