{"task_id": "django_044", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "serena", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "Native duration support is determined by the database connection\u2019s `features` object:\n\n- [`django/db/backends/base/features.py`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/backends/base/features.py:84) defines `BaseDatabaseFeatures.has_native_duration_field = False`. Backends therefore default to emulated duration storage.\n- [`django/db/backends/postgresql/features.py`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/backends/postgresql/features.py:16) overrides it to `True`.\n- [`django/db/backends/oracle/features.py`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/backends/oracle/features.py:27) also overrides it to `True`.\n- MySQL and SQLite inherit `False`.\n\n`DurationField` resolves storage through the normal field-to-backend type mapping:\n\n1. [`DurationField.get_internal_type()`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:1941) returns `\"DurationField\"`.\n\n2. The inherited [`Field.db_type()`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:889) uses that string to look up `connection.data_types[\"DurationField\"]`.\n\n3. Each backend supplies its implementation:\n\n   - PostgreSQL: `interval` in [`postgresql/base.py`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/backends/postgresql/base.py:114)\n   - Oracle: `INTERVAL DAY(9) TO SECOND(6)` in [`oracle/base.py`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/backends/oracle/base.py:134)\n   - MySQL: `bigint` in [`mysql/base.py`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/backends/mysql/base.py:119)\n   - SQLite: `bigint` in [`sqlite3/base.py`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/backends/sqlite3/base.py:74)\n\nThe value-conversion path mirrors that distinction:\n\n- [`DurationField.get_db_prep_value()`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:1964) delegates writes to `connection.ops.adapt_durationfield_value()`.\n- The base implementation in [`base/operations.py`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/backends/base/operations.py:589) converts a `timedelta` to integer microseconds, matching MySQL/SQLite `bigint` storage.\n- PostgreSQL and Oracle override that adapter to return the `timedelta` unchanged, allowing their drivers to bind native interval values.\n- On reads, [`DurationField.get_db_converters()`](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-serena-django-django/django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:1967) adds `connection.ops.convert_durationfield_value` only when native support is absent. The base converter reconstructs `datetime.timedelta` from the stored microsecond integer.\n\nThus, the feature flag governs native-versus-emulated conversion behavior, while `connection.data_types`, selected through `get_internal_type()` and `Field.db_type()`, determines the actual backend column type.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 9, "relevance": 10, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 35066, "output_tokens": 1330, "total_tokens": 36396, "cache_read_tokens": 79360, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 6, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": [], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "serena", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "serena", "server_name": "serena", "launch_command": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/serena.exe", "launch_args": ["start-mcp-server", "--project", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-serena-django-django", "--transport", "stdio", "--enable-web-dashboard", "false", "--enable-gui-log-window", "false"], "serv