{"task_id": "django_045", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "c0-bare", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "The intercepted implementation is `Query.add_q()` on the base SQL `Query` class:\n\n- Defined in [django/db/models/sql/query.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/db/models/sql/query.py:1662)\n- Class defined as `class Query(BaseExpression)` in the same file at line 231.\n- Specialized SQL query classes such as `DeleteQuery`, `UpdateQuery`, `InsertQuery`, and `AggregateQuery` inherit this implementation through `Query`; they do not override `add_q()`.\n\nThe tests import that exact class with:\n\n```python\nfrom django.db.models.sql import Query\n```\n\nand patch it in [tests/prefetch_related/tests.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/tests/prefetch_related/tests.py:393):\n\n```python\nadd_q = Query.add_q\nmock.patch.object(Query, \"add_q\", ...)\n```\n\nThe deferred path begins on `QuerySet`, which is a separate wrapper rather than a subclass of SQL `Query`. Its `query` property materializes `_deferred_filter` by calling `_filter_or_exclude_inplace()` in [django/db/models/query.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-c0-bare-django-django/django/db/models/query.py:344). That function ultimately invokes:\n\n```python\nself._query.add_q(Q(...))\n```\n\nat line 1679, reaching the patched base implementation in `django.db.models.sql.query.Query`.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 9, "relevance": 9, "clarity": 8, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 19632, "output_tokens": 982, "total_tokens": 20614, "cache_read_tokens": 90624, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 5, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["django\\\\db\\\\models\\\\query.py", "django\\\\db\\\\models\\\\sql\\\\query.py", "tests/prefetch_related/tests.py", "tests\\\\prefetch_related\\\\tests.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "c0-bare", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "c0-bare", "server_name": null, "launch_command": null, "launch_args": null, "served_tools": null, "client_tools": [], "index": null, "shares_index_with": null, "hooks_declared": [], "isolation": "worktree", "tree": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-c0-bare-django-django"}, "served_tools": [], "served_count": null, "mcp_tools_issued": [], "mcp_isError_count": 0, "arm_exercised": null, "mcp_per_server": {}, "hook_events": null, "hook_injections": null, "index_evidence": {}, "models_used": ["gpt-5.6-sol"], "prompt_style": "neutral", "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5", "wall_clock_seconds": 44.46574568748474, "index_time_seconds": 0.0, "judge_time_seconds": 6.884310722351074, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.045688, "error": null, "timed_out": false, "retries": 0, "timestamp": "2026-08-05T15:53:19.397163+00:00", "prompt_sent": "Answer the following question about this code repository.\nBe specific and reference actual code files and functions.\n\nQUESTION: Where in the Query class hierarchy is the add_q method implementation that gets intercepted by the mock patch to verify deferred filtering behavior?\n\nThink step by step. Use the available tools to explore the codebase.", "model_used": "gpt-5.6-sol", "session_id": "", "stop_reason": "", "duration_api_ms": 44464, "repo_commit": "3b161e60964a", "raw_output_file": "logs\\layerb_codex_bakeoff_django\\raw_outputs\\django_045_c0-bare.json"}
{"task_id": "django_045", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "repowise", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "The intercepted implementation is directly on the base SQL `Query` class:\n\n- `Query` is defined as `class Query(BaseExpression)` in [django/db/models/sql/query.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/django/db/models/sql/query.py:231).\n- `Query.add_q()` is implemented on that same class in [django/db/models/sql/query.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/django/db/models/sql/query.py:1662). It preprocesses the filter, calls `_add_q()`, adds the resulting clause to `self.where`, and handles join demotion.\n- Specialized SQL query classes such as `DeleteQuery`, `UpdateQuery`, `InsertQuery`, and `AggregateQuery` inherit from this `Query` in [django/db/models/sql/subqueries.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/django/db/models/sql/subqueries.py:17), but they do not provide the implementation being patched.\n\nThe deferred-filter tests import `Query` through `django.db.models.sql` and patch the base-class method with `mock.patch.object(Query, \"add_q\", ...)` in [tests/prefetch_related/tests.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/tests/prefetch_related/tests.py:388) and again at [tests/prefetch_related/tests.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-repowise-full-django-django/tests/prefetch_related/tests.py:1130).\n\nSo the hierarchy is:\n\n`BaseExpression \u2192 Query`, with `add_q()` defined on `Query`; the mock intercepts that concrete base implementation.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 9, "relevance": 10, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 35615, "output_tokens": 1038, "total_tokens": 36653, "cache_read_tokens": 153088, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 4, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["django/db/models/query.py", "django/db/models/sq