{"task_id": "django_045", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "code-review-graph", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "The intercepted implementation is `Query.add_q()` on the SQL-level base class:\n\n- Defined in [django/db/models/sql/query.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/models/sql/query.py:1662) as `django.db.models.sql.query.Query.add_q`.\n- `Query` itself inherits from `BaseExpression`; `add_q()` is not implemented on `QuerySet` or a subclass.\n\nThe deferred-filtering path is:\n\n1. `QuerySet.query` applies the saved filter via `_filter_or_exclude_inplace()` in [django/db/models/query.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/django/db/models/query.py:345).\n2. `_filter_or_exclude_inplace()` calls `self._query.add_q(...)` at line 1677 or 1679.\n3. `self._query` is normally an instance of the SQL `Query` class, constructed at line 330.\n4. The tests patch that exact base-class method with `mock.patch.object(Query, \"add_q\", ...)` in [tests/prefetch_related/tests.py](C:/Users/ragha/Desktop/bakeoff/lb-code-review-graph-django-django/tests/prefetch_related/tests.py:396) and again at line 1135.\n\nSo, in hierarchy terms, the mock intercepts the implementation directly on the base SQL `Query` class\u2014not a `QuerySet` method or an override in `DeleteQuery`, `UpdateQuery`, `InsertQuery`, or `AggregateQuery`.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 8, "completeness": 7, "relevance": 9, "clarity": 8, "reasoning": 8}, "input_tokens": 17831, "output_tokens": 934, "total_tokens": 18765, "cache_read_tokens": 82432, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 4, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": ["django\\\\db\\\\models\\\\query.py", "django\\\\db\\\\models\\\\sql\\\\query.py", "django\\\\db\\\\models\\\\sql\\\\subqueries.py", "tests\\\\prefetch_related\\\\tests.py"], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_cal