{"task_id": "django_045", "benchmark": "swe_qa", "condition": "serena", "repo": "django/django", "question_type": "django", "resolved": null, "answer": "The intercepted implementation is defined directly on the base `Query` class\u2014not on a specialized subclass:\n\n- [`django/db/models/sql/query.py:1662`](C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-serena-django-django/django/db/models/sql/query.py:1662): `Query.add_q(self, q_object, reuse_all=False)`\n- `add_q()` preprocesses the condition, delegates to `self._add_q(...)`, adds the resulting clause to `self.where`, and performs join demotion.\n\nThe deferred-filtering tests patch that exact class method:\n\n- [`tests/prefetch_related/tests.py:393`](C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-serena-django-django/tests/prefetch_related/tests.py:393)\n- [`tests/prefetch_related/tests.py:1134`](C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-serena-django-django/tests/prefetch_related/tests.py:1134)\n\nThey first save `Query.add_q`, then use `mock.patch.object(Query, \"add_q\", autospec=True, ...)`. The mock intercepts calls while its `side_effect` invokes the saved original implementation, allowing the tests to assert that deferred filtering ultimately calls `Query.add_q` exactly once.", "judge_scores": {"correctness": 9, "completeness": 9, "relevance": 10, "clarity": 9, "reasoning": 9}, "input_tokens": 16698, "output_tokens": 809, "total_tokens": 17507, "cache_read_tokens": 97792, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "num_tool_calls": 4, "num_turns": 1, "task_subagent_calls": 0, "files_explored": [], "files_edited": [], "repowise_tools_called": [], "server_tools_called": {}, "attach_guard_fired": null, "token_source": "codex:turn.completed.usage", "category": "", "arm": "serena", "arm_provenance": {"arm": "serena", "server_name": "serena", "launch_command": "C:\\Users\\ragha\\.local\\bin/serena.exe", "launch_args": ["start-mcp-server", "--project", "C:\\Users\\ragha\\Desktop\\bakeoff\\lb-serena-django-django", "--transport", "stdio", "--enable